PVD("uruguay_vision_2019-2050",{"docs":["","Uruguay National Development Plan till 2050"],"s":{"1":[[1,"9","5","Short- and Medium-Term Productive Policy Roadmaps","These conclusions are also articulated with the construction of short- and medium-term policies on productive issues developed through Transforma Uruguay.",""],[1,"11","2","Participatory Strategic Foresight Methodology","Foresight seeks to systematize and structure relevant information on a topic that is dispersed among multiple actors.",""],[1,"20","3","National Social Dialogue Process","the social dialogue, which aimed to develop a series of participatory meetings (during 2016) that would make it possible to think about Uruguay's future on strategic issues",""],[1,"20","6","Interactive State-Society Development Planning Process","Development planning should result from an interactive process between these two actors, with the aim of identifying strategic priorities to ensure sustainable development in the long term.",""],[1,"22","3","Strategic Foresight and Scenario Planning","Anticipating these phenomena through foresight, designing different scenarios and approximating their probability of occurrence, establishing strategies to take advantage of opportunities or defend against threats, is the core of modern planning.",""],[1,"23","4","National Strategic Planning Guidelines","This document advances the formulation of guidelines for national strategic planning.",""],[1,"23","5","Strategic Framework for Future Public Plans","Therefore, this Development Strategy 2050 proposes to frame the future plans of the different public agencies.",""],[1,"26","3","Participatory Strategic Foresight Process","a process of anticipating and exploring expert opinion from networks of people and institutions in government, businesses and universities, in a structured, interactive, participatory, coordinated and synergistic manner, to build strategic visions […] of a country's development.",""],[1,"26","4","National Foresight and Scenario Planning Process","Foresight was used as an instrument to identify and articulate possible, probable and desirable futures for sustainable national development.",""],[1,"26","5","Strategic Foresight and Policy Decision Support Process","These processes seek to examine the present and understand possible futures, integrating research findings from different fields of knowledge, multidisciplinary perspectives, and knowledge from different qualified social actors throughout the process.",""],[1,"26","6","Prospective Studies Governance Group Formation","Prospective studies began with the design of the process and the formation of governance groups.",""],[1,"27","7","Strategic Action Mapping and Policy Recommendation Process","The strategic map consists of public policy recommendations to advance toward the target scenario.",""],[1,"27","8","Strategic Review and Foresight Monitoring Mechanism","Finally, it is necessary to generate instruments for the periodic review of the strategic lines, putting active prospective monitoring into practice, which also implies defining indicators for monitoring and the spaces responsible for these actions.",""],[1,"27","9","State-Level Strategic Planning System Consolidation","The consolidation of a strategic planning system at the state level is one of the medium-term actions that would strengthen development planning and the use of foresight tools.",""],[1,"27","9","Coordination of Planning and Foresight Systems","Better coordination between foresight, strategic planning, and the different levels of five-year and operational planning would ensure greater coherence and efficiency of public policies.",""],[1,"253","2","Participatory Prospective Scenario Planning","Two workshops with broad participation from organized civil society, academia, and the public and private sectors were held, in which the axes were defined and scenarios for 2030–2050 were constructed.",""]],"2":[[1,"58","4","Social Protection Matrix Consolidation","It is necessary to accompany productive transformation with the consolidation of a denser social protection matrix.",""],[1,"58","4","Societal Capacity Development for Demographic and Technological Change","It is necessary to improve society's capacities to interact with demographic change and increasingly advanced technologies.",""],[1,"185","2","Societal Capacity Development for Demographic and Technological Change","It is necessary to improve society's capacities to interact with demographic change and increasingly advanced technologies.",""],[1,"58","4","Broad Distribution of Productivity Gains","It is necessary to develop actions that ensure the broad social distribution of the productivity gains associated with productive transformation.",""],[1,"58","5","Universal Social Protection Architecture","The consolidation of a universal social protection architecture by 2050 is set as a goal.",""],[1,"59","2","Lifelong Public Services Expansion","Public services of excellence, with broader offers that cover the entire population throughout people's lives and enable them to develop their capabilities to the fullest.",""],[1,"59","2","Retraining During Employment Disaffiliation","Periods of employment disaffiliation should be used for retraining, without affecting the family's standard of living or the continuity of the education—or other social services—of their daughters and sons.",""],[1,"59","2","Strengthening of Non-Contributory Social Protection","All this requires strengthening the non-contributory pillar of social protection, progressively equalizing its benefits with those of the contributory pillar.",""],[1,"75","15","Higher Education Access Expansion Programme","especially by greatly expanding access to higher education",""],[1,"76","7","Worker Retraining and Reintegration Support Services","provider of social services that enable the retraining and reintegration of large contingents of workers",""],[1,"80","2","Tertiary Education Access Expansion","The improvement in educational levels—and, in particular, the massification of access to tertiary education—appears to be the best response to the automation process under way globally.",""],[1,"80","8","Ambitious Labour Reskilling Plans","the need for ambitious labour reskilling plans for those workers who must redirect their labour-market integration",""],[1,"80","8","Expanded Competency Certification Systems","the need to expand competency certification systems for current and future workers who do not reach the levels of formal education that will be required",""],[1,"102","3","Lifelong Learning and Workforce Adaptation Support","This means that the education system and the labour market must be able to respond to the challenges of updating knowledge and lifelong education, to support workers in this process.",""],[1,"102","5","Labour Market Adaptation and Reskilling Strategy","An adaptation strategy should be adopted to anticipate and respond to labour market changes based on new tasks and knowledge promoted by environmental sustainability.",""],[1,"102","5","Green Employment Promotion Strategy","It is necessary to implement a strategy to promote green employment by designing policies and plans to stimulate the incorporation of green jobs and people with that profile into the labour market.",""],[1,"102","8","Waste Picker Socio-Productive Inclusion and Formalization","The Waste Bill currently under consideration by Parliament provides for the socio-productive inclusion of waste pickers through processes of labour formalization and competency certification.",""],[1,"173","2","Regulatory Reform for Universal Social Protection","These paths must be accompanied by a regulatory readjustment that guarantees social protection for all people, regardless of their form of work.",""],[1,"185","2","Social Protection System Consolidation","It is necessary to accompany productive transformation with the consolidation of a denser social protection matrix, which counterbalances the concentrating trends observed in the world.",""],[1,"187","2","2050 Social Protection Architecture Restructuring","The 2050 social protection architecture must acknowledge these changes and restructure itself to address emerging inequalities and vulnerabilities.",""],[1,"187","8","Universal Social Protection System","A universal protection system, financed with general taxes and general revenues and in which access to benefits does not depend on the person's (or their family's) link to the labor market, seems to be the best response to a productive-labor scenario.",""],[1,"188","2","Universal Social Protection Matrix","Having a universal social protection matrix implies that public policies guarantee that all citizens have equal conditions of access, adequacy and quality of social services, benefits and provisions, regardless of where they live, their sex, age, work or income.",""],[1,"190","10","Domestic Work Labour Law and Implementing Decree","Law 18065 on domestic work and Decree 224/2007.",""],[1,"223","3","General Employment Law and Labor Protection Reform","It is imaginable to establish a general employment law that ensures minimum protections for all forms of work and conventional labor law with greater protections for subordinated work.",""],[1,"223","4","Universal Lifelong Social Protection System","We must imagine a new social contract that provides universal social protection throughout life, with a basic level for all vulnerable people, complemented by contributory social security schemes that provide higher levels of protection.",""],[1,"224","7","Worker Social Protection Investment","Increased investment in social protection for workers, regardless of contractual type",""],[1,"225","3","Universal Social Protection Floor","A social protection floor that offers a basic level of protection to all those who need it.",""],[1,"225","3","Contributory Social Insurance Schemes","Contributory social insurance schemes that provide higher levels of protection.",""],[1,"225","4","Progressive Taxation Models for Technology-Generated Wealth","This will force us to think of models built on a tax base that taxes the greater wealth produced, as a counterpart to the exclusion from that same wealth that new technologies and automation will generate.",""],[1,"241","5","Uruguay Social Protection System Reform","Therefore, it is necessary to profoundly transform the architecture of Uruguay's social protection, with the goal of reducing inequalities and increasing the population's capabilities to navigate a world full of challenges.",""],[1,"246","2","Flexible Access Requirements for Contributory Social Protection","Make requirements for accessing the contributory pillar of social protection more flexible",""],[1,"246","3","Flexible Eligibility for Contributory Social Protection","Progress gradually by making requirements more flexible for entering contributory arrangements or accessing some of their benefits.",""],[1,"246","3","Contribution Subsidies for Social Security and Health Insurance","Generate contribution subsidies in insurance systems—basically social security and health—to provide protection to sectors being left outside the contributory system.",""],[1,"246","4","Non-Contributory Social Protection Strengthening and Expansion","Strengthen and extend the non-contributory pillar of social protection.",""],[1,"246","5","Non-Contributory Social Protection Pillar Strengthening","In the long term, however, the goal should be to strengthen the non-contributory pillar so that it can constitute the basis of the social protection system.",""],[1,"246","6","Integrated Basic and Contributory Pension Scheme","At retirement, a basic pension or universal transfers could be combined with contributions to a solidarity fund or individual capitalization, derived from pension systems.",""],[1,"244","2","Labour Protection Mechanisms for Platform Workers","Develop labour protection mechanisms that take into account the situation of platform workers, as well as other new forms of work.",""],[1,"244","3","Universal Social Protection for Non-Standard Workers","It is also necessary to consider workers who work remotely or have flexible schedules, which are increasingly common, and ensure basic social protection conditions for all workers, whether subordinate, semi-autonomous, or independent.",""]],"3":[[1,"60","4","Gender-Equal Sharing of Unpaid Care Responsibilities","promote shared responsibility between men and women in unpaid domestic tasks",""],[1,"60","4","Public Policies Addressing the Care Crisis","public policy mechanisms that address the care crisis",""],[1,"60","5","Gender-Responsive Social Risk Policies","policies that address social risks whose consequences fall primarily on women",""],[1,"220","3","Gender Gap Reduction Policy","The reduction of gender gaps is emerging as one of the two main social responses to the effects of demographic change on the labor market, the economy, and social security.",""],[1,"237","3","Uruguay Care Policy","Uruguay's care policy aims to promote the development of autonomy among people in situations of dependency, and their care and assistance, through shared responsibility among families, the State, the community and the market.",""],[1,"237","4","Integrated Care and Autonomy Policy","Based on the law creating the National Integrated Care System and the National Care Plan 2016-2020, the exercise of a new right is being included in the welfare matrix.",""],[1,"237","5","Care Services under the National Integrated Care System","The system is articulated around five components: care services.",""],[1,"237","5","Caregiver Training Programme","The system is articulated around five components: training of caregivers.",""],[1,"237","5","Care Services and Labour Regulation","The system is articulated around five components: regulation of services and labour.",""],[1,"237","5","Care Information and Knowledge Management System","The system is articulated around five components: information and knowledge management.",""],[1,"237","5","Care System Communication Mechanism","The system is articulated around five components: communication.",""],[1,"237","6","Work and Study Reconciliation Care Centres","Devices that enable reconciliation between study or work and care, such as centres in unions and companies (SIEMPRE)",""],[1,"237","6","Care Centres for Students' Children","Devices that enable reconciliation between study or work and care, such as centres for the children of students",""],[1,"237","7","National Integrated Care System","Law 19353. Creation of the National Integrated Care System.",""],[1,"237","9","National Care Plan 2016-2020","National Care Plan 2016-2020.",""],[1,"241","3","Socialized and Redistributed Care Work Policies","This requires policies that promote the socialization and redistribution of care work between men and women, and also among families, the State, the community and the market.",""],[1,"241","7","Parental and Care Leave Improvement","Continue improving maternity, paternity, breastfeeding and care leave in general.",""],[1,"241","7","Family Care Co-Responsibility Policies","Policies that stimulate co-responsibility in care within families.",""],[1,"242","5","Female Labour Force Participation Expansion","Promote the expansion of female labour force participation",""],[1,"242","6","Female Labour Force Participation Promotion Policy","A first option to prevent the decline in the activity rate resulting directly from ageing is to promote the continuation and deepening of the growth trend in female activity rates.",""],[1,"242","7","National Integrated Care System Expansion","It is essential to advance policies such as the expansion of the SNIC (now in all its components and not only in early childhood).",""],[1,"242","7","Intra-family Care Co-responsibility Measures","the adoption of measures that promote progress in intra-family co-responsibility for care, helping to reduce the burden of unpaid work that falls on women",""],[1,"242","7","Cultural Change for Gender Equality","continue promoting cultural advances that have modified the traditional conception of women solely as housewives",""],[1,"242","7","Women’s Education and Skills Development Policies","policies that contribute to increasing women's educational and qualification levels",""],[1,"247","3","Care Work and Women's Employment Reconciliation Policies","Additionally, it is necessary to continue advancing state policies that help shift care work toward services or reconcile both time commitments with women's participation in employment (for example, through leave, flexibility strategies or mechanisms promoting parental care).",""],[1,"247","3","Flexible Early Childhood Care Services Expansion","In particular, it is important to assess the possibility of expanding more flexible care service options for the first year of life that could operate outside the hours of existing services, as well as cover the work schedules of workers with non-standard hours, for example during weekends or at night.",""],[1,"247","3","Elderly and Dependent Persons Care Services","Similarly, it is necessary to develop a broad range of services focused on caring for the elderly and dependent population, in line with the efforts already initiated through SNIC.",""],[1,"255","6","Co-responsibility Policy Implementation","through the implementation of co-responsibility policies",""],[1,"277","3","National Integrated Care System Construction","Both themes are currently being addressed in the process of building the National Integrated Care System.",""],[1,"278","6","State Care Services and Benefits Provision","The State must provide services and benefits to help resolve care needs and enable better reconciliation between family and work responsibilities for men and women.",""],[1,"278","6","Labour Market Reform for Family Care Responsibilities","A change in the labour market must also be promoted so that the ideal worker model transforms into one of workers with family and care responsibilities.",""],[1,"278","6","Company Adaptation for Work and Care Responsibilities","Companies will also have to adapt their functioning to eliminate the tensions that undermine quality care.",""],[1,"278","7","Health, Education and Social Security Systems Adaptation Reform","Health, education and social security systems must adapt to these changes, and recognize that care work is essential for the sustainability of life.",""],[1,"280","3","Care Co-Responsibility Policy","with co-responsibility policies in care",""],[1,"280","11","Domestic and Care Work Valuation Policy","Promoting the valuation of domestic and care work.",""],[1,"281","4","Shared Care Responsibilities Policy","Promote shared responsibility in care.",""],[1,"281","9","Domestic and Care Work Redistribution Policy","Recognize and redistribute domestic and care work, a pillar of social well-being.",""],[1,"281","10","Universal Care System Expansion","Adopt measures to strengthen and extend the care system so that it achieves universal coverage.",""],[1,"281","10","Public Care Infrastructure Development","Create and improve public care infrastructure for children, older persons, or persons with disabilities.",""],[1,"281","11","Society-Wide Co-Responsibility for Care","Establish co-responsibility for care throughout society, integrating the State, the market, the community and families.",""],[1,"281","11","Nationwide Quality Care Services Expansion","This includes expanding and strengthening quality care responses throughout the national territory.",""],[1,"281","11","Caregiver Professionalization and Skills Recognition","This includes the professionalization and recognition of the knowledge of people who provide care.",""],[1,"281","11","Promotion of Men’s Participation in Care","This includes promoting men’s participation in care, among other actions.",""],[1,"282","2","Work-Family Reconciliation and Shared Care Measures","implement measures to promote the reconciliation of family and work life through shared responsibility",""],[1,"282","3","Domestic and Care Work Valuation and Support Measures","Value the domestic and care work sector, and generate support measures to eradicate care work performed by girls and adolescents.",""]],"4":[[1,"92","3","National Climate Change Policy","The National Climate Change Policy (PNCC), with a horizon to 2050, is a broad and cross-cutting policy whose general objective is to promote adaptation to and mitigation of climate change in Uruguay.",""],[1,"92","3","Transport Emissions Mitigation and Energy Efficiency","Mitigation of emissions from the transport sector through increased efficiency and the combination of energy sources.",""],[1,"92","3","Climate Adaptation in Productive Systems","Strengthening adaptation to climate variability and climate change in industrial, mining, commercial and service production systems.",""],[1,"92","3","Waste and Wastewater Emissions Mitigation","Mitigation of greenhouse-gas emissions arising from waste management and wastewater treatment.",""],[1,"94","3","REDD+ Forest Emissions Reduction Preparation Programme","The Programme for Preparation for Reducing Emissions from Deforestation and Degradation of native forest (REDD+ project).","MVOTMA | MGAP"],[1,"94","10","REDD+ Forest Emissions Reduction Programme","The objective of REDD+ is to reduce GHG emissions from deforestation and degradation processes, as well as maximize opportunities to increase carbon stocks in Uruguay's native forests.",""],[1,"134","5","Coastal Zone Climate Mitigation and Adaptation Policies","Effective mitigation and adaptation policies in the coastal zone.",""],[1,"294","14","National System for Response to Climate Change and Variability","National System for Response to Climate Change and Variability (SNRCC).",""]],"5":[[1,"94","3","National Biodiversity Conservation and Sustainable Use Strategy","The strategic guidelines for protecting and improving the state of biodiversity are addressed in the National Strategy for the Conservation and Sustainable Use of Biological Diversity in Uruguay.","MVOTMA"],[1,"94","3","National Native Forest Strategy","The approach to native forest is the subject of the National Native Forest Strategy.","MGAP"],[1,"290","26","National Native Forest Strategy","MGAP. National Native Forest Strategy. 2018.","MGAP"],[1,"94","3","National and International Biodiversity Conservation Area Strengthening","Strengthening national and internationally recognized biodiversity conservation areas.",""],[1,"94","3","Biodiversity Mainstreaming in Planning and Land-Use Management","The incorporation of biodiversity into planning and land-use management processes, as well as into sectoral plans for productive activities.",""],[1,"94","3","Native Forest Maintenance and Restoration Strategy","A strategy for maintaining and restoring native forest.",""],[1,"119","10","Sustainable Management of Planted and Native Forests","through sustainable forest management of both planted forest and native forest",""],[1,"121","6","Native Forest Conservation and Sustainable Valuation","Part of sustainable forest management is based on the conservation and valuation of native forest, making appropriate use of ecosystem services and non-timber products.",""],[1,"121","6","Native Forest Public Awareness and Citizen Engagement","It also consists in informing, raising awareness and involving citizens regarding the importance and benefits of native forest.",""]],"6":[[1,"94","5","Environmental Strategic Guidelines Development","advance towards the elaboration of strategic guidelines",""],[1,"95","2","Environmental and Productive Agenda Coordination Mechanism","to articulate that environmental agenda with the productive agenda derived from this 2050 Development Strategy, guaranteeing its sustainability.",""],[1,"95","4","Promotion of Sustainable Productive Activities","Identify and promote productive activities aligned with sustainable resource management that combine greater added value with higher environmental quality.",""],[1,"99","2","Environmental Quality Food Certification Incentive Mechanism","Finally, from the public sector, mechanisms should be evaluated to incentivize environmental quality certification processes for food.",""],[1,"99","3","Resource Optimization and Waste Valorization Initiative","Resource optimization and waste valorization within a circular economy",""],[1,"99","4","Ecodesign and Product Environmental Impact Reduction","It could also be considered to move toward ecodesign by incorporating recyclability and reducing environmental impact into product design.",""],[1,"99","4","Initiatives to Extend Product Useful Life","Other dimensions of the circular economy that are progressively being developed are initiatives seeking to increase the useful life of goods.",""],[1,"99","5","Environmental Awareness and Education Programme","It seems essential to advance society’s environmental awareness and education, focusing on the need to transform consumption and disposal habits.",""],[1,"99","5","Waste Valorization Production Processes","It is essential to advance productive processes for waste valorization, which enable the recirculation of materials and prevent the excessive consumption of resources.",""],[1,"99","6","National Waste Valorization Knowledge and Dissemination","the need to increase knowledge and dissemination about processes and technologies for waste valorization at the national level",""],[1,"99","7","Applied Technologies for Environmental Control and Management","Technologies applied to environmental control, monitoring and management",""],[1,"99","8","Sectoral Environmental Best Practice Guidelines","The preparation of sectoral guidelines is proposed, defining common guidelines for incorporating best practices and technologies adapted to the national context.",""],[1,"99","8","Promotion Mechanisms for Cleaner Technologies","The development of mechanisms to promote the incorporation of new, more efficient and less polluting technologies is proposed, through instruments such as training, technical support, loans, tax benefits, and quality awards, among others.",""],[1,"101","7","Resource Consumption and Pollution Reduction Policy","Promueve la reducción del consumo de energía y de materias primas, así como las emisiones de GEI, la generación de residuos y la contaminación, y favorece la protección de los ecosistemas.",""],[1,"104","9","Sustainable Natural Resource Transformation and Product Diversification","The country's natural resource base should be strongly oriented toward the transformation of products and processes in the direction of sustainable production, and toward venturing into the production of new goods based on them.",""],[1,"153","6","Circular Economy Transition","The circular economy proposes a radical systemic change aimed at ecodesign and industrial symbiosis.",""],[1,"154","2","Circular Production and Consumption Model","A production and consumption model based on optimizing resource use throughout the production chain, minimizing waste generation, and multiplying internal loops after the consumption stage.",""],[1,"154","3","Ecodesign Integration","Ecodesign, that is, the integration of environmental aspects into the design and development of a product with the aim of reducing adverse environmental impacts and improving its environmental performance throughout the life cycle.",""],[1,"154","3","Product Life Extension through Maintenance, Repair and Remanufacturing","They involve maintenance, repair and remanufacturing.",""],[1,"154","3","Recycling, Composting and Resource Valorization","The strategies are based on giving resources a new life through recycling, composting and other types of valorization, such as energy valorization.",""],[1,"154","4","Circular Economy Resource Efficiency and Waste Valorization Initiative","The creation of new productive opportunities, goods and services associated with optimizing resource use and valorizing waste is proposed.",""],[1,"154","5","Circular Opportunities 2017 Programme","The creation of the Circular Opportunities 2017 programme is highlighted, with the objective of promoting the validation of ideas, the launch of new business lines, and the implementation of projects that promote a transition toward the circular economy.",""],[1,"154","6","Circular Economy Action Plan","Transforma Uruguay is preparing the first Circular Economy Action Plan, whose general objective is to promote the circular economy within the country's sustainable development.",""],[1,"154","6","Waste Valorization Policy Strengthening","This is one of the strategies of the first National Plan for Productive Transformation and Competitiveness, prepared in 2016, which proposes strengthening public policies for this purpose.",""],[1,"154","6","Integrated Waste Management Legislation","In June 2018, the Executive submitted to Parliament a bill on Integrated Waste Management that proposes significant changes to waste management at the national level.",""]],"7":[[1,"171","8","Expansion of Tertiary Education Participation","An increasing number of young people should attain tertiary education.",""],[1,"171","8","Creative and Interdisciplinary Pedagogical Proposals","The national education system, at its three levels, should retain and engage adolescents and young people through pedagogical proposals that promote creativity, imagination, flexibility and interdisciplinarity.",""],[1,"173","2","Creative and Innovative Capacity Development in Education","It is necessary to strengthen the development of creative, innovative and proactive capacities within the formal education system, at all three levels.",""],[1,"173","2","Secondary Education Retention and Tertiary Access Initiative","It is even more important to create the conditions to reduce dropout in secondary education and enable a larger number of young people to access tertiary education.",""],[1,"173","2","Education-to-Work Linkage Mechanism","It is also necessary to strengthen the coordination between study and work at all levels.",""],[1,"178","10","Project-Based Pedagogical and Curricular Strategies","Promote, in coordination with the relevant bodies, pedagogical and curricular strategies that challenge children and adolescents, particularly by fostering project-based teaching with cross-cutting themes to creatively and collaboratively solve real problems affecting young people and their communities.",""],[1,"178","11","Alternative Secondary Education Completion Programme","Specific programmes for workers who left secondary education early to complete cycles and continue their educational pathway, through tailored plans using accelerated and distance-learning modalities and by accrediting knowledge and competencies acquired at work.",""],[1,"178","12","Teacher Science and Innovation Training Programme","Strengthen training in the natural and human sciences for primary and secondary education teachers in teacher-training institutions.",""],[1,"178","13","Secondary Education Retention and Tertiary Access Policies","These instruments should be complemented by a set of public policies that would reduce dropout levels in secondary education and enable a growing number of young people to access tertiary education.",""],[1,"179","3","Public Higher Education Options Expansion","Continue expanding the range of public education options, through both Udelar and UTEC, promoting greater mobility, transdisciplinarity, and techno-creative profiles, and encouraging young people to innovate, imagine, create, take risks, and make mistakes.",""],[1,"179","4","UTEC Consolidation and Research Capacity Programme","Promote the consolidation of UTEC through the creation of research groups and the promotion of full-time dedication among its teachers.",""],[1,"179","6","Scientific Dissemination and Public Understanding Instruments","Promote scientific dissemination, designing instruments that enable citizens to understand the main global and local challenges.",""],[1,"179","14","Intensive Immersion Skills Development Programme","These are intensive immersion strategies, generally lasting a few days or weeks, that seek to develop specific skills in a subject, both in technological matters and in social innovation or skills development.",""],[1,"231","2","Secondary Education Completion Improvement","the need to improve completion rates in secondary education",""],[1,"231","2","Tertiary Education Access and Completion Expansion","the need to continue expanding access to and completion of tertiary education",""],[1,"231","9","Compulsory Education Requirement","The LGE establishes initial education from age 4, primary education, and lower and upper secondary education as compulsory (Article 6).",""],[1,"233","3","University-Level Teacher Education Reform","A relevant challenge at this level concerns completing the process of giving teacher education a university character that integrates the university functions of teaching, research and extension.",""],[1,"234","2","Extended Pedagogical Time Models","Models that promote the extension of pedagogical time (full-time or extended-time)",""],[1,"234","2","Community Teachers Programme","The Community Teachers Programme at the primary level",""],[1,"234","3","Curriculum Improvement Initiatives","This is contributed to by the curriculum improvement initiatives being implemented for early childhood education as well as primary and secondary education, which aim towards a more open and flexible curriculum design that helps improve students’ navigation through the education system, taking into account their interests and motivations.",""],[1,"234","4","Integrated Educational Pathways and Accreditation Reform","An improvement in coordination between subsystems would generate an integrated system focused on the learner, enabling them to choose among varied pathways and have knowledge acquired across different levels and modalities recognized through accreditation mechanisms.",""],[1,"234","5","Interinstitutional Tertiary Education Access and Infrastructure Initiative","Greater coordination should also promote access to tertiary education through modalities such as those already being implemented between CETP-UTU of ANEP, Udelar and UTEC for the implementation of inter-institutional training proposals and the shared use of infrastructure.",""],[1,"234","5","Upper Secondary Education Curriculum and Optionality Reform","In connection with this, there is a need to move beyond viewing upper secondary education solely as a requirement for entering university programmes, as well as its subject-based tendency and low optionality.",""],[1,"234","7","Broad-Based Foundational Education Approach","The relevance of broad-based foundational education is highlighted, avoiding hyperspecialization that reduces flexibility to adapt to new changes.",""],[1,"234","9","National Curriculum Reference Framework","In 2017, the National Curriculum Reference Framework (MCRN) was published, establishing stage profiles and graduation profiles that define the learning students are expected to achieve at each stage of their educational trajectory.",""],[1,"236","3","Knowledge Democratization and Research Capacity Expansion","Expanding people's capabilities requires democratizing knowledge, taking advantage of the potential arising from generalizing advanced training and multiplying research and innovation capacities to produce more and, above all, better goods and services, prioritizing the needs of the most disadvantaged, with a much more frugal and sustainable use of natural resources.",""],[1,"236","4","Universal Secondary Education for Work and Advanced Learning","Universalize secondary education that prepares both for decent work and for continuing advanced learning.",""],[1,"236","5","Flexible Secondary Education Completion Programme","It is essential and also viable to organize educational offerings that guarantee those who complete secondary education training that enables them both to work with dignity and productivity and to continue studying successfully at the tertiary level.",""],[1,"236","6","Secondary Education Teacher Training Programme","Universalizing such secondary education should guide teacher training.",""],[1,"236","6","Secondary Education Pedagogical Renewal","Universalizing such secondary education should guide pedagogical renewal.",""],[1,"236","6","Secondary Education Curriculum Reform","Universalizing such secondary education should guide curricular changes.",""],[1,"236","6","Secondary Education Institutional Development","Universalizing such secondary education should guide institutional creations.",""],[1,"236","6","Secondary Education Resource Allocation","Universalizing such secondary education should guide resource allocation.",""],[1,"236","7","Permanent Tertiary Education Expansion","Generalize permanent tertiary education",""],[1,"236","8","Lifelong Education and Vocational Training Programmes","For this purpose, lifelong education and vocational training programmes must be prioritized, linking and orienting them towards expanding access to tertiary education.",""]],"8":[[1,"19","6","SDG Agenda Mainstreaming Actions","The Office of Planning and Budget has promoted and led actions to position the SDGs on the national political agenda.","Office of Planning and Budget | National Institute of Statistics | Uruguayan Agency for International Cooperation"],[1,"19","6","Integrated SDG Monitoring and Follow-Up System","Together with the National Institute of Statistics and the Uruguayan Agency for International Cooperation, they coordinated efforts to establish systems for monitoring and following up on SDG indicators, integrated with national planning.","Office of Planning and Budget | National Institute of Statistics | Uruguayan Agency for International Cooperation"],[1,"19","9","SDG Action Monitoring and Coordination Mechanism","Presidential Resolution 988/16 entrusted OPP with monitoring and coordinating actions associated with the SDGs.",""],[1,"19","9","International Cooperation Coordination Mechanism","Presidential Resolution 988/16 entrusted AUCI with matters related to international cooperation.",""],[1,"19","9","SDG Indicator Development and Data Collection","Presidential Resolution 988/16 entrusted INE with the preparation and collection of indicators.",""],[1,"20","2","SDG Policy and Institutional Mapping Reports","It should be noted that these reports offer, in addition to statistical information associated with indicators, a mapping of public policies and the institutional and regulatory framework, and a survey of citizen participation spaces related to each reported SDG.",""],[1,"20","4","SDG-Convergent National Action Planning","planning actions convergent with the SDGs",""],[1,"20","4","Public Spaces and Instruments for SDG Ownership","generating appropriate spaces and instruments to facilitate society's ownership of the SDGs",""],[1,"20","4","Collective Capacity-Building Initiative","developing and strengthening collective capacities",""],[1,"20","4","Consensus-Building and Leadership Mechanism","building consensus and leadership for implementing plans in specific socio-territorial contexts",""]],"9":[[1,"56","2","Environmental Sustainability Integration into Productive Planning","The planning of productive transformation must be undertaken with regard to the need for environmental sustainability.",""],[1,"57","6","National Sustainable Bioeconomy Strategy","Uruguay is currently designing its National Sustainable Bioeconomy Strategy, in which several of these issues will be considered in its strategic guidelines.","Sustainability and Climate Change Unit of MGAP | DP-OPP | MIEM | MEF | MVOTMA | TU"],[1,"91","9","Uruguay Climate Projections and Agricultural Adaptation Planning","Climate projections for Uruguay to 2040 and 2070 using the statistical downscaling technique under the National Adaptation Plan for the agricultural sector, OPYPA, MGAP, forthcoming.","MGAP"],[1,"92","3","Agricultural Land-Use and Soil-Management Plans","Implementation of land-use and soil-management plans.",""],[1,"92","3","Sustainable Natural Grassland Management","Sustainable management of natural grassland.",""],[1,"92","3","Climate Insurance for Agriculture","Climate insurance.",""],[1,"92","3","Climate-Efficient Agricultural Technologies","Adoption of technologies that enable improved efficiency of systems.",""],[1,"92","3","Carbon-Sequestering Land Management and Afforestation","Strengthening management practices that enable carbon sequestration, such as forestation.",""],[1,"93","2","Sustainable Intensification Policy","The Ministry of Livestock, Agriculture and Fisheries (MGAP) promotes a policy in which one of the strategic axes is sustainable intensification.","Ministry of Livestock, Agriculture and Fisheries (MGAP)"],[1,"93","2","Soil Use Planning and Control","Planning and control in the use and management of soils.","Ministry of Livestock, Agriculture and Fisheries (MGAP)"],[1,"93","2","Responsible Agrochemical Use and Control","The responsible and controlled use of agrochemicals.","Ministry of Livestock, Agriculture and Fisheries (MGAP)"],[1,"93","2","Good Agricultural Practices Strengthening","Strengthening good agricultural practices for the farming sector.","Ministry of Livestock, Agriculture and Fisheries (MGAP)"],[1,"152","3","Uruguay Agrointeligente Sustainable Production Platform","The Uruguay Agrointeligente platform seeks productive intensification with economic, environmental and social sustainability, adaptation to and mitigation of climate change, and promotion of competitiveness and international integration, among others.","MGAP"]],"10":[[1,"57","1","Value-Added Food Production Upgrading","That implies the need for product differentiation—that is, to overcome the commodity characteristic of many of them—and to achieve, based on high quality, high technology, natural production certifications respectful of the environment and animal welfare, access to higher and more stable prices.",""],[1,"89","6","Specialized Market Access Strategies for Non-Traditional Services","Develop differentiated and specialized strategies for market access by non-traditional services.",""],[1,"89","6","Diversification of Non-Traditional Services Export Destinations","At the same time, work should be done to diversify the destinations of these exports, in order to make them less vulnerable and generate new opportunities.",""],[1,"89","7","Long-Term Export Market Access Policy","Consolidate access for national products to the main destination markets, such as China, overcoming the primary-product bias in the current relationship.",""],[1,"90","2","Export Destination Diversification Strategy","Develop strategies to avoid overdependence on a single destination.",""],[1,"90","3","South American Trade Consolidation Policy","The implementation of a more active policy in this regard, overcoming the bilateral perspective and design that still prevail.",""],[1,"90","4","Sub-Saharan Africa and South Asia Trade Relations Programme","Deepen trade relations with Sub-Saharan Africa and South Asia.",""],[1,"90","5","Investment Attraction and Product Valorization Incentive Policy","Consider, in international integration, active incentive policies to attract investments and add value to products and services.",""],[1,"91","2","International Trade Rules and Dispute Settlement Policy","Promote the revaluation of international trade rules.",""],[1,"144","7","Halal Certification Recognition Programme","Therefore, it is understood that work should be done on this certification so that it is recognized in all markets.",""]],"11":[[1,"93","4","Water Ecosystem Preservation Measures","These are based on measures for the preservation of ecosystems in river basins and aquifers.",""],[1,"93","4","Water Impact Mitigation Measures","These are based on measures for mitigating impacts in river basins and aquifers.",""],[1,"93","4","River Basin and Aquifer Ecosystem Restoration","These are based on measures for restoring ecosystems in river basins and aquifers.",""],[1,"93","4","Integrated Water Resources Planning","They are based on integrated water resources planning.",""],[1,"93","4","Water Information Systems","They are based on establishing information systems for water bodies.",""],[1,"93","4","Water Body Monitoring Networks","They are based on establishing monitoring networks for water bodies.",""],[1,"98","3","Water Footprint Measurement in Agro-Export Production","It is recommended to anticipate possible international market requirements and begin implementing this measure in the country's production processes, in order to consolidate efficient and traceable water management.",""]],"12":[[1,"100","2","National Environmental Observatory","The creation of the National Environmental Observatory (OAN) under the authority of MVOTMA.","MVOTMA"],[1,"100","2","Real-Time Environmental Monitoring for Large Enterprises","The incorporation by Dinama of online, continuous and real-time monitoring of the environmental variables of large enterprises.",""],[1,"100","4","Environmental Technology Research and Development Support","In this regard, R&D processes related to technologies for environmental control, monitoring and management may be supported and promoted.",""],[1,"100","5","Sector Assessment for Environmental Technological Reconversion","Regarding the demand for technology for sustainability, it may be useful to survey and prioritize the sectors in which the need for technological reconversion to reduce environmental impact is anticipated.",""],[1,"100","6","Bioremediation Knowledge Development Initiative","The development of knowledge to seek bioremediation solutions (application of biological processes to restore a damaged environment) is also a path to study from a medium- and long-term perspective.",""],[1,"100","7","Strategic Environmental Assessment Integration Mechanism","Strategic environmental assessments (SEAs), which seek to deepen the incorporation of the environmental dimension into the design of public policies, plans and development-related projects, constitute a suitable instrument in this regard.",""],[1,"100","10","National Environmental Information Centralization Platform","It is an open-access platform that centralizes environmental information to provide inputs for institutional decision-making and disseminate information to the population.","MVOTMA"],[1,"102","6","Environmental Protection Economic Instruments Pillar","Development of a pillar of economic instruments for environmental protection",""],[1,"102","7","Environmental Economic Instruments Policy","However, internationally, there is a trend towards incorporating economic instruments, complementarily with regulatory schemes.",""],[1,"103","2","Green Taxation Instrument","Within the framework of economic instruments, green taxes are imposed on an activity, practice or product that generates a negative environmental impact, so that the more intensive that practice or activity is, the more it must pay in tax, thereby creating an incentive for the producer to reduce that impact.",""],[1,"103","3","Plastic Bags Regulatory and Economic Instrument","The Plastic Bags Law combines regulatory instruments (it limits the manufacture and import of single-use plastic bags to those that are biodegradable or compostable) and economic instruments (it also establishes the obligation for actors in the commercialisation chain to charge for them and sets a minimum price for authorised bags).",""],[1,"103","4","Low-Impact Production Incentive Instruments","These instruments can become incentives for productive development in inputs or production processes with low environmental impact, becoming a tool serving sustainable development.",""],[1,"103","5","Environmental Economic Instruments Intensification","the need to intensify the use of economic instruments applied to environmental management, understood here in a broad sense (green taxes, fiscal incentives, subsidies and tax deductions), as a complement to the existing regulatory instruments.",""],[1,"129","8","Environmental Standards Development and Enforcement","Description, adaptation and enforcement of environmental standards in Uruguay, aiming for the best international standards applicable to national industry.",""]],"13":[[1,"111","3","Cross-Sectoral ICT Application Development Initiative","The most promising and most relevant productive ICT development vector for the country as a whole is the development of applications specifically designed to meet the needs of the other productive complexes.",""],[1,"111","3","Transversal ICT Capacity Strengthening Guidelines","The following section presents fundamental strategic guidelines for strengthening capacities for the transversal development of ICT.",""],[1,"111","9","Data Regulation and Information Protection Framework","There is optimal regulation on data that allows broad availability of data, with multiple interoperable databases and a strong information protection policy.",""],[1,"112","3","Intelligent Infrastructure Development for Digital Access","The development of intelligent infrastructures that facilitate the availability of technologies and access to fundamental platforms for future productive and social development.",""],[1,"112","3","Multi-Actor and Cross-Sector Coordination Capacity","The development of capacities for coordination among multiple actors and multiple sectors.",""],[1,"112","3","Data Management Regulation Framework","The development of data management regulation capacities that enable Uruguayan society to obtain greater benefits and security from digitalization.",""],[1,"112","5","Intelligent Infrastructure Access Development","To achieve the ICT 2050 scenario, Uruguay must develop access to what is called intelligent infrastructures, a set of interconnected infrastructures that will form the basis of productive and social development in the near future.",""],[1,"112","7","IoT and 5G Connectivity Infrastructure Expansion","Particularly enhance the connectivity of the Internet of Things (IoT) and the 5G network.",""],[1,"112","9","Scalable Cloud Computing and Storage Infrastructure","Cloud infrastructures that enable the availability of flexible and scalable computing and storage capacity as a service through the network.",""],[1,"113","5","National Data Infrastructure Development","Develop data infrastructures covering repositories for open data, including the functionalities required to comply with personal data protection regulations and tools for managing and monetizing private data.",""],[1,"113","9","Internet of Things Infrastructure Development","Internet of Things infrastructure",""],[1,"113","10","Connected Objects and Real-Time Data Platform Integration","These cover the connectivity already mentioned, but go further to integrate the entire value chain, from the deployment and management of connected objects—and, in particular, sensors—to the capture of data and its real-time processing on data and artificial intelligence platforms to facilitate application deployment.",""],[1,"114","2","Connected Objects Decision-Making and Control Mechanism","It integrates mechanisms for decision-making and control of connected objects so that they perform certain actions.",""],[1,"114","5","Cybersecurity Infrastructure and Data Protection Initiative","Cybersecurity infrastructure and data protection",""],[1,"114","6","Cybersecurity Infrastructure Defense Initiative","Consequently, cybersecurity infrastructures must provide defenses against a multitude of circumstances, types of attack, and possible points of attack.",""],[1,"114","8","Innovation Networks and Articulation Platforms","Promote innovation networks through articulation-mediation platforms, enabling a given actor to easily learn about other innovations relevant to its objectives and facilitating their integration.",""],[1,"115","5","Data Acquisition and Circulation Regulation","Regulation plays a fundamental role in achieving highly fluid acquisition and controlled circulation of data.",""],[1,"116","2","Data Regulation and Governance Framework","It is necessary to advance data regulation, seeking, on the one hand, the greatest possible circulation and use of open data and, on the other, generating controls that ensure due privacy and trust.",""],[1,"116","3","Data Source Integration and Interoperability Mechanism","This requires ensuring the availability of data relating to integration and interoperability between heterogeneous data sources to facilitate access and value creation through the transversal use of these sources.",""],[1,"116","3","Open Data Policy","This therefore includes open data policies.",""],[1,"116","3","Data Protection Policy","This therefore includes data protection policies.",""],[1,"116","4","Regulatory Sandbox Innovation Framework","The possibility of introducing regulatory sandboxes that foster innovation should also be evaluated.",""],[1,"116","4","Cross-Sectoral and Ex Post Regulatory Reform","It appears necessary to move towards cross-sectoral regulations, involving various sectors, and possibly ex post regulations.",""],[1,"116","4","Artificial Intelligence Regulation and Liability Framework","It is also necessary to advance regulation on artificial intelligence and the liabilities that may arise from its use.",""],[1,"116","6","Ex Post Antimonopoly Compliance Validation","Validate ex post that actors' behavior does not infringe the country's general objectives, such as antimonopoly objectives.",""]],"14":[[1,"115","3","Remote Digital Health Monitoring Mechanism","In health, different solutions facilitate the remote monitoring of people with certain diseases.",""],[1,"115","3","Automated Emergency Health Coordination Mechanism","It is possible to coordinate, when considered necessary, the arrival of a mobile emergency unit at the person’s location, prepare the hospital to which the person will be taken, arrange the specialized services required, allocate the bed where the person will be placed, and manage traffic in the smart city to avoid additional delays.",""],[1,"115","4","Higher Education and Training Innovation Integration","Higher education and training should be articulated with all actors in society in a fluid manner, enabling the integration of education and training activities with their work and, eventually, cultural activities.",""]],"15":[[1,"117","7","Road Access Improvement to Export Ports","In the near future, it is key to reduce the cost of moving products to ports by road.",""],[1,"117","7","Railway System Reactivation","In the near future, it is key to reduce the cost of moving products to ports through the reactivation of the railway system.",""],[1,"117","7","Fluvio-Maritime Port System Strengthening","It is also necessary to strengthen the fluvio-maritime port system.",""]],"16":[[1,"119","10","Promotion of New Business Ecosystems","and promotes the emergence of new business ecosystems",""],[1,"119","14","Integrated Wood Residue Energy Utilization Programme","The use of by-products and wood waste for energy, integrated with the forestry chain, complements the country's renewable energy matrix.",""],[1,"120","6","Investor and Business Engagement Initiative","Encourage investors and companies to become involved in specific areas.",""],[1,"120","7","Network Creation Promotion Initiative","Promotion of the creation of networks for use",""],[1,"120","10","Entrepreneurship and Forest Management Skills Support","Support for entrepreneurship and competencies in forest management",""],[1,"120","12","Creation of an Attractive Operational Environment for EWP","Creation of an attractive operational environment for EWP*",""],[1,"120","13","Pulp Product Diversification Initiative","Diversify the types of pulp produced",""],[1,"120","14","Competitive Product Adaptation Initiative","Adapt competitive products in EWP to international requirements",""],[1,"120","15","Eucalyptus Pulp Product Development Support","Support national actors to develop new eucalyptus pulp products",""],[1,"120","16","Local Pulp-Based Paper and Cardboard Production Promotion","Promote the production of certain specific types of paper and cardboard from local pulp.",""],[1,"120","17","Secondary Pulping Flow Bioproduct Investment","Invest in new bioproducts from secondary pulping flows.",""],[1,"120","19","Sawmill Bark Materials and Chemical Applications Development","Development of materials and chemical applications using bark available in sawmills",""],[1,"120","20","Industrial-Site Heat and Energy Production","Enhance the production of heat and energy at the sites where industry is installed",""],[1,"120","21","Conversion of Secondary Wood Flows into Solid Biofuels","Convert secondary wood flows into solid biofuels that are easy to store",""],[1,"120","24","Forest Sector Investment Promotion Policy","This requires designing exclusive investment promotion policies for the most dynamic segments.",""],[1,"120","24","Forest Sector Investor and Alliance Identification","and identifying key investors, as well as potential alliances for the development of the sector.",""],[1,"121","2","Forestry Industry By-Product Utilization Networks","It is key to promote the creation of networks for the use of by-products, residues and waste (secondary streams) from the forestry industry.",""],[1,"121","2","Industrial Park Promotion for Mechanical Transformation","The mechanical transformation industry could be strengthened through the promotion of industrial parks.",""],[1,"121","3","Forest Plantations and Logistics Efficiency Investment","Maximize the value of the existing forest resource base through efficient use of plantations and infrastructure and logistics.",""],[1,"121","3","Integrated Forestry and Complementary Activities Programme","Optimize forest resources also through combining plantations with other activities (agriculture, livestock, beekeeping, tourism).",""],[1,"121","3","Alternative Forest Freight Transport Analysis","Analyze forms of transport alternative to road transport (rail and maritime).",""],[1,"121","5","Forest Management Entrepreneurship and Skills Support","Supporting entrepreneurship and competencies in forest management creates the conditions for sustainable forest management and quality biomass availability.",""],[1,"121","5","Local Forestry Entrepreneurship Networks","It is necessary to create networks of local entrepreneurs, supporting capacity development and ensuring the logistics infrastructure necessary for the development of new ventures.",""],[1,"121","5","Forestry Logistics Infrastructure Development","Ensuring the logistics infrastructure necessary for the development of new ventures.",""],[1,"121","8","Local and Regional Engineered Wood Products Market Development","For this purpose, it is necessary to develop a local and regional market for engineered wood products (Engineered Wood Products, EWP).",""],[1,"122","2","Structural Wood Certification and Standardization System","establishing a certification and standardization system for structural wood",""],[1,"122","2","Legal Framework Review for Wood Construction","reviewing the legal framework concerning regulations that limit wood construction",""],[1,"122","3","Structural Wood Certification and Market Access Initiative","Certification of structural wood through standardized regulations is imperative, a path the country is already undertaking.",""],[1,"122","7","Integrated Pulp and Bioproduct Plant Development","These initiatives can be promoted through the development of integrated plants for pulp and by-products, paper and packaging.",""],[1,"122","7","Biorefinery Process Integration in Large-Scale Mills","These initiatives can be promoted by adding biorefinery processes to large-scale pulp and paper mills.",""],[1,"122","8","Specialized Paper and Cardboard Production Development","The production of certain specific types of paper and cardboard should be promoted, using local pulp and developing local cases of technological applications capable of creating high-value-added by-products.",""],[1,"122","8","Pulp, Biomaterials and Biorefinery Innovation Platform","Supporting national actors to develop new eucalyptus pulp products, creating a joint innovation platform for the different types of pulp, paper and biomaterials, and biorefinery.",""],[1,"123","3","Cellulose-Based Packaging and Textile Production","The substitution of petrochemical plastic, driven by environmental problems and changes in consumer behavior, is presented as a clear opportunity for the cellulose industry to evolve toward the production of containers, packaging, and textiles.",""],[1,"123","5","Bioproduct Investment from Secondary Pulping Flows","Investing in new bioproducts from secondary pulping flows would allow the separation of lignin and hemicellulose from pulp processing operations and their subsequent transformation into intermediate and final products.",""],[1,"123","6","Chemical Industry Entry Incentive Scheme","Incentivizing the entry of this type of company",""],[1,"123","6","Chemistry and Biotechnology Skills Development","Creating key competencies in chemistry and biotechnology",""],[1,"123","8","Biomass Industrial Clusters and Parks Development","Develop industrial clusters and parks (for example, around sawmills) to enhance heat and energy production at the sites where the industry is established, through public-private partnerships to achieve optimal use of resources, linking municipal operations.",""],[1,"123","9","Solid Biofuel Production Initiative","An opportunity that is becoming clearer consists of producing easily stored solid biofuels from wood-processing residues—pellets, briquettes and others—with a new solid biofuel offering.",""],[1,"124","3","Second-Generation Biofuel Production Exploration","Explore opportunities for the production of second-generation biofuels from forest biomass, including hydrogen and advanced fuels such as renewable diesel.",""],[1,"124","3","Advanced Biorefinery Development Partnerships","Promote partnerships between cellulose plants, circular economy initiatives and ANCAP for the joint development of advanced biorefineries.",""]],"17":[[1,"126","3","Technology Roadmapping and Future Scenario Planning Study","The study identifies the key variables of the system and some technology roadmaps, distinguishing emerging technologies, markets and products, and proposes prioritizing them by configuring four future scenarios.",""],[1,"127","5","Future Technologies Prioritization Policy","Prioritization of certain “future technologies”",""],[1,"127","10","Distribution Network Planning Software Development","In the medium-term horizon (2025), good opportunities are envisioned for the development of distribution network planning software.",""],[1,"127","10","Photovoltaic Generation Forecasting Software Development","In the same horizon, conditions are foreseen for the development of photovoltaic generation forecasting software.",""],[1,"127","10","National Energy Demand Management Solutions","In the same horizon, conditions are foreseen for the development of hardware and software solutions for the optimal management of national energy demand.",""],[1,"128","2","Development of Materials for Energy-Efficient Construction","The development of new materials and components for efficient construction will enable the emergence of companies providing advice on building modelling for energy efficiency.",""],[1,"128","3","Wind Power Prediction and Grid Voltage Control Technologies","In terms of distribution and transmission, in the short term, opportunities are foreseen for the development of technologies for predicting and controlling wind power, as well as for voltage control in the grid.",""],[1,"128","3","Real-Time Adjustable Electricity Tariff System","These technologies are necessary to provide tariffs that can be adjusted in real time, according to the reality of variable generation.",""],[1,"128","3","Smart Meter Deployment for Electricity Consumers","In the medium term, the incorporation of smart meters for all consumers is envisaged, which will make it possible to measure and remotely understand demand behavior.",""],[1,"128","3","Remote Appliance Management and Electric Vehicle Integration","In addition, the use of remotely manageable appliances (Internet of Things) and the incorporation of electric vehicles will make it possible to manage practically 100% of electricity demand.",""],[1,"128","3","Large-Scale Energy Data Management","Opportunities for development associated with the management of data on a large scale (big data) are envisaged.",""],[1,"128","3","Personal and Energy-System Data Security","Opportunities for development associated with the security of personal data and data from the operation of the system are envisaged.",""],[1,"128","4","Wind Energy Control and Maintenance Technology Adaptation","Opportunities are expected for adapting technology in control and maintenance systems.",""],[1,"128","4","Renewable Energy Storage and Demand Management Development","The high presence of non-dispatchable or variable renewable energies will point toward the development of battery storage systems, pumped-storage and turbine plants, and demand management.",""],[1,"128","5","Biomass Residue Supply and Logistics Development","In the short term, opportunities are seen in the supply and logistics of agricultural, forestry and agro-industrial residues, toward better utilization for energy generation.",""],[1,"128","5","Biorefinery Development for Biofuels and Biomaterials","In the long term, the identified trends point toward the development of biorefineries to obtain biofuels, biomaterials and other products.",""],[1,"128","7","Renewable Energy Innovation by Public Energy Companies","Within the target scenario, the objective has been set for these companies to remain at the forefront of renewable resource use, promoting and developing new products and services.",""],[1,"128","8","Research, Development and Innovation Promotion","Promote the generation of research, development and innovation (R&D&I).",""],[1,"128","9","Renewable Energy Research and Innovation Programme","Promotion of the generation of basic and applied knowledge in the renewable energy sector, at both public and private levels",""],[1,"129","2","Regional and International Research Partnership Programme","regional and international partnership for the development of research",""],[1,"129","2","Private-Sector R&D&I Investment Promotion","investment in R&D&I by private enterprise",""],[1,"129","2","Sectoral Research and Development Fund Strengthening","strengthen existing funds, such as the energy sectoral fund",""],[1,"129","2","Postgraduate Professional Hiring Incentive Mechanism","generate economic mechanisms to encourage the hiring in private companies of professionals with postgraduate training",""],[1,"129","2","International Research Institute Linkage Incentive","incentivize links with institutes abroad",""],[1,"129","2","Renewable Energy Research and Development Institutes","the creation of institutes and development centers dedicated to R&D&I in renewable energies",""],[1,"129","2","Local Knowledge Adoption Incentives for Businesses","incentives for companies that incorporate knowledge developed locally",""],[1,"129","3","Renewable Energy Goods and Services Production Capabilities","Develop capabilities to produce goods and services linked to renewable energies",""],[1,"129","4","Renewable Energy Products and Services Development","Aim to generate high-value-added products and services linked to renewable energies that position the country as a benchmark for the regional market.",""],[1,"129","4","Long-Term Science and Technology Policy for Energy Inputs","This requires a long-term science and technology policy that enables the emergence and development of an energy-input industry with export capacity and local supply.",""],[1,"129","10","Energy Efficiency Campaigns","On the state side, energy efficiency campaigns have been implemented",""],[1,"129","10","Electric Public and Taxi Transport Transition","and a change in the transport matrix, shifting to electric vehicles for both taxis and buses",""]],"18":[[1,"126","7","Energy-Resilient Housing for Vulnerable Households","the establishment of energy-resilient homes for one hundred percent of vulnerable households",""],[1,"129","5","Household Energy Resilience Development Policy","Promote social development through energy resilience in households",""],[1,"129","6","Healthy and Energy-Resilient Housing Provision","It involves ensuring the production of healthy and energy-resilient housing for vulnerable households.",""]],"19":[[1,"132","2","Comprehensive Tourism Training Programme","This process is accompanied by the implementation of a comprehensive tourism training programme, which includes transversal skills (languages, ICT tools, culture, environment) and soft skills (such as creativity, teamwork, resilience, proactivity, among others).",""],[1,"132","4","Integrated Tourism Destination Management","integrated management of destinations",""],[1,"132","4","Tourism Accessibility Plans","the adoption of accessibility plans",""],[1,"132","4","Tourism Investment Promotion","the stimulation of diverse investments",""],[1,"132","5","Thematic and Structured Tourism Offer Development","Uruguay consolidates a thematic and structured tourism offer adapted to the demands of the new type of tourist.",""],[1,"132","5","Community-Based Tourism Resource Valorization","This resulted from systematic work to identify and analyse tangible and intangible tourism resources in the territories, revalue them and enhance their tourism value, with the participation of the local community.",""],[1,"132","6","Systematic Tourist Profile Research Programme","A process of consolidating systematic research on tourist profiles",""],[1,"132","6","Segment-Based Tourism Promotion and Marketing Strategy","The generation of dynamic promotion and marketing tools adapted for each segment",""],[1,"132","8","Tourism Education and Hospitality Skills Programme","Incorporation into curricula and school and secondary-school programmes of basic tourism concepts ... as well as transversal competencies of a host through playful and creative tools, and programmes that enable experiencing tourism from early childhood.",""],[1,"132","8","National Cultural Icons Tourism Branding Initiative","Enhancement of the value of cultural icons ... as supports for positioning the national tourism brand.",""],[1,"133","2","Local Production and Traditions Tourism Inventory","Deepening the processes of inventorying local production and traditions, and analysing their tourism potential.",""],[1,"133","2","Integrated Local Product Tourism Offer","Ensuring the sustainability of programmes to revalue these local products and strengthening them through the formation of an integrated offer that responds to the demands of different tourist segments.",""],[1,"133","2","Community-Based Heritage Projects","Promotion of identity-based heritage projects with community-based management.",""],[1,"133","2","Tourism and Local Production Value Chain Integration","Strengthening the interconnection of tourism with local production chains, structuring offers of premium local products that sustain the Uruguay Natural brand promise.",""],[1,"133","4","Quality Tourism Education and Skills Development Programme","Strengthening a quality educational offer that incorporates not only the development of transversal skills, but also tourism agenda topics.",""],[1,"133","4","Permanent Online Tourism Training Platforms","Consolidation of permanent online training platforms to ensure access to the continuous updating of talent throughout the national territory.",""],[1,"133","4","Public-Private-Academic Tourism Information Institution","Design of a public-private-academic institution to generate joint information and improve decision-making in terms of public policies and private strategies for the development of the sector.",""],[1,"133","4","Tourism Research Chairs","Promotion of the establishment of research chairs on priority tourism issues and their link with national development.",""],[1,"133","6","Specialized Tourism Infrastructure Provision","Provision of differentiated, specific and specialized infrastructure for tourism.",""],[1,"133","6","Priority Tourism Product Investment Incentive Policy","Policy to stimulate investments in prioritized tourism products and connectivity infrastructure linking public and private actors.",""],[1,"133","6","Integrated Mobility-as-a-Service Transport Programmes","Implementation of integrated transport programmes adopting a mobility-as-a-service approach.",""],[1,"133","6","Interregional Tourism Connectivity Infrastructure","Provision of transversal infrastructure enabling connections between thematic tourism products in different regions.",""],[1,"133","6","International Transport Connection Points","Development of international connection points in the center, south and north of the country, interconnected with local transport.",""],[1,"134","2","Air Passenger Transport Attraction Instruments","Generation of instruments to attract passenger air transport to improve this type of connectivity.",""],[1,"134","2","Integrated Accessibility Plans for Priority Destinations","Integrated accessibility plans implemented and operational in all prioritized destinations (for example, universally accessible beaches).",""],[1,"134","3","Local Management Training and Professionalization Programme","Training and professionalization of local managers.",""],[1,"134","3","Integrated Destination Planning Instruments and Joint Planning Mechanism","Development of integrated destination planning instruments and joint and continuous planning instances that make it possible to build common agendas linking local and national spheres.",""],[1,"134","3","Institutionalized Public-Private Destination Management Bodies","Institutionalized, professional public-private management bodies with a budget for destination management.",""],[1,"134","3","Public Interinstitutional Coordination for Integrated Local Policies","Public interinstitutional coordination bodies that design and implement integrated public policies in localities.",""],[1,"134","3","Professionalized Private Sector Strategic Planning Coordination","Professionalized private coordination bodies that support the sector's strategic planning.",""],[1,"134","5","Sustainability and Ecosystem Awareness Education Programmes","Implementation of educational and awareness programmes around the culture of sustainability, resilience and local ecosystems.",""],[1,"134","5","Green Tourism and Local Value Policy Integration","Incorporation into public policies of the interrelationship between culture, local value and green tourism, as well as the potential of emerging technologies to strengthen it.",""],[1,"134","5","Sustainable Nature-Based Tourism Enterprise Promotion","Deepening of instruments to promote development projects for tourism enterprises consciously integrated with nature and society, and economically sustainable.",""],[1,"134","5","Integrated Ecosystem Care and Recovery Programmes","Integrated ecosystem care and recovery programmes, with a focus on watershed protection and water quality.",""],[1,"134","5","Sustainable Management of Tourist Localities","Sustainable management in tourist localities across the country.",""],[1,"135","3","Tourism Research and Innovation Centres","Development of research and innovation centres on tourism agenda topics, focusing on the profiles of tourists attracted or targeted.",""],[1,"135","3","Real-Time Tourism Statistics System","Provision of up-to-date real-time statistical data on the actors in the productive network to support the structuring of supply according to prioritized audience segments.",""],[1,"135","3","Joint Sustainable Tourism Promotion Mechanism","Generation of mixed tourism promotion forums that, using the inputs produced by research, define joint instruments to sustain a distinctive sustainable tourism positioning and develop the destination's own competitive advantages.",""]],"20":[[1,"135","5","Strategic Map for Innovative Industry Development","To develop and strengthen these industries, encourage the production of innovative, high-quality and internationalizable goods and services, with integrated value chains and committed public-private leadership, a strategic map was prepared to outline some of the main sets of actions to achieve their development.",""],[1,"135","7","Integrated Prospective Governance Mechanism","For this purpose, an integrated governance structure comprising MIEM, DNI, Dinapyme, Dinatel, MEC (through DICAU and DNC), Uruguay XXI, IMM, ANII, ANTEL and OPP met throughout the prospective process.","Ministry of Industry, Energy and Mining (MIEM) | Ministry of Education and Culture (MEC)"],[1,"138","2","International Market Placement for Creative Services and Products","It refers to placing services and products in the international market, positioning the country as a creative provider.",""],[1,"138","2","International Sales Platform and Export Partnership Development","This implies flexibility to take advantage of sales platforms already developed in other countries, as well as partnerships with others, both local and international.",""],[1,"138","2","Creative Sector Event Development","Create events.",""],[1,"138","2","Public and Private Sector Investment in Creative Exports","Invest from the public and private sectors.",""],[1,"138","2","Creative Industry Human Resources Training","Train human resources.",""],[1,"138","2","Creative Export Manuals and Protocols","Create manuals and protocols.",""],[1,"138","2","International Event Monitoring and National Event Creation","Survey international events and create national events for these purposes.",""],[1,"138","4","Creative Skills-Oriented Formal Education","Formal education should be oriented toward this objective.",""],[1,"138","4","Multidisciplinary Team Formation Initiative","The stimulation of the formation of multidisciplinary teams should be oriented toward this objective.",""],[1,"138","4","Youth Participation Promotion","The participation of young people is configured as a key element in this regard.",""],[1,"138","4","Women’s Inclusion in Decision-Making","The visibility and place of women in decision-making spaces are configured as key elements in this regard.",""],[1,"138","6","Integrated Sector Governance and Innovation Coordination Mechanism","It aims to create a space where public and private actors engage in dialogue with a holistic view of the sector, a governance forum made up of business chambers, ministries, institutes and agencies, tasked with coordinating existing policies, minimizing bureaucratic bottlenecks, pooling funds for innovation, and generating performance and evaluation indicators, operating protocols, and useful sectoral information.",""],[1,"138","7","Cross-Sectoral Linkage Mechanism for National IICC Sectors","It requires periodic meetings among stakeholders, the training of mediating agents, the development of a business culture, support and alliances.",""],[1,"138","8","Creative Industries Human Capital Development Programme","It means emphasizing the preparation of people to improve their creative potential as well as their business prospects, with more and better innovative tools linked to digital and entrepreneurial activities.",""],[1,"139","2","Creative Industries Strategic Map","The purpose of this map is to chart a route of actions to achieve a robust and dynamic creative industries system in the long term.",""],[1,"140","2","Creative Industries Information System","Node 1. Information system for creative industries",""],[1,"140","3","Cultural and Creative Industries Information System","Collect and systematize what Uruguay has to offer in cultural and creative industries for events in the rest of the world, while organizing and prioritizing these offerings.",""],[1,"140","3","Sectoral Funding and Performance Monitoring Mechanism","Maintain a permanent survey of funds and support for each sector, and generate performance indicators and continuous reports by sector.",""],[1,"140","5","National Creative Industries Market and Showcase","Strengthen a national event that allows some of the experiences of Uruguay's creative industries to be showcased to the region and the world.","Ministry of Education and Culture"],[1,"140","7","Creative Industries Innovation and Collaboration Support","This node is intended to underpin the creative processes behind each product or service in these industries.",""],[1,"140","8","University Agreements for Cultural and Creative Education","It aims to seek specific agreements with universities that have tertiary-level programmes related to cultural management, the arts, and creative fields, so that educational pathways can be incorporated into them.",""],[1,"140","9","Creative Industries Observatory","The creation of an Observatory of Creative Industries is planned.",""],[1,"141","2","Cross-Industry Business Linkage Development","Forming and having linkers (human resources responsible for establishing bridges between the various industries), facilitating business opportunities and, in turn, the professional consolidation of sales agents for the products and services created, at national and international level.",""],[1,"141","2","Multidisciplinary Training and Trainer Development","Training opportunities are sought from a multidisciplinary perspective, which implies the primary need to train trainers in multidisciplinary teams.",""],[1,"141","4","Creative Industries Interinstitutional Coordination Mechanism","It involves creating a formal space for interinstitutional coordination that articulates what happens around the creative industries.",""],[1,"141","5","Creative Industries Development Deepening Initiative","Creative industries have undergone a series of positive changes in recent years that require further deepening involving all actors participating in decision-making.",""],[1,"141","8","Thematic Commissions and Working Groups Mechanism","The Ministerial Cabinet for Productive Transformation and Competitiveness may create thematic commissions or working groups when justified for this purpose.","Ministerial Cabinet for Productive Transformation and Competitiveness"]],"21":[[1,"97","6","Environmentally Sustainable Food Differentiation Strategy","The production of traceable foods certified as environmentally sustainable would be a strategy for Uruguay to anticipate or rapidly adapt to possible environmental requirements of international markets.",""],[1,"98","6","Sectoral Studies on Environmental Export Requirements","It is necessary to generate information—through sectoral studies—about the possible impact that evolving environmental requirements may have on the main national food export chains and on adaptation mechanisms.",""],[1,"98","7","Environmental Quality Food Production Standards and Certification Framework","It is considered necessary to establish and disseminate a common framework of definitions and standards for food production processes with environmental quality, from which certifications adapted to national circumstances and consistent with the requirements of the main export markets can be developed.",""],[1,"98","9","Grassland Meat Certification Programme","Grassland Meat, a certified meat programme produced under the protocol defined by the Grassland Alliance",""],[1,"98","9","Uruguay Certified Natural Meat Programme","The Uruguay Certified Natural Meat Programme of the National Meat Institute (INAC) allows certification of the meat production process through compliance with a protocol",""],[1,"142","6","Technology-Based Biomass and Resource Value Chain Development","This requires focusing on technological processes that make it possible to fully harness the availability of biomass and existing resources.",""],[1,"146","7","Meat Processing Automation and Technology Adoption","The current challenges involve adapting technology for the stages of meat processing that are more difficult to automate (for example, deboning) and continuing the process of incorporating it for those that are simpler to automate: from secondary packaging onward (picking, storage, loading, etc.).",""],[1,"147","2","Industrial Information and Data Skills Training","It will be necessary to train people to manage information, use the data generated to make the process increasingly efficient and improve decision-making.",""],[1,"147","2","Video Image Processing for Industrial Classification","The use and processing of video images is possibly the most disruptive technology to be incorporated, with the objective of identifying and classifying valuable cuts on the line.",""],[1,"147","3","Environment-Based Livestock Systems Development","This will enable the development of environment-based livestock systems by applying the information collected on feed use.",""],[1,"147","3","Personnel Training for Technology Interaction","There is a need to make significant efforts in training personnel to interact with technology, both at the primary and industrial levels.",""],[1,"147","4","Natural Products Value Proposition Development","Uruguay should deepen its value proposition based on natural products to supply high-value markets.",""],[1,"147","4","Sustainable Production and Animal Welfare Market Positioning","It is therefore relevant that Uruguay continue positioning itself and improving its image on issues that may increase its competitive advantage in the markets it targets: environmentally sustainable processes and animal welfare.",""],[1,"147","5","Local Cold-Chain Distribution Network Agreements","In particular, agreements are required to create local distribution networks responsible for the logistical aspects that guarantee product distribution with an adequate cold chain and ensure transaction formality.",""],[1,"148","2","Data Analysis Workforce Training Programme","For data analysis, a much more highly trained workforce must be developed.",""],[1,"148","4","Workforce Reconversion and Redeployment for Dairy Automation","It is necessary to define reconversion and redeployment processes so as not to generate inefficiencies in work.",""],[1,"148","6","Oilseed Production Information and Environmental Management System","There must be more information on where planting takes place and management must be adjusted by environment.",""],[1,"148","6","Public Technology Generation Incentives for Oilseed Production","Public incentives are considered necessary through active policies to generate more technology, as is also the case in the dairy sector.",""],[1,"148","6","Technical Capacity Training for Oilseed Technology","It is also necessary to scale up and improve the training of technical capacities associated with the technological needs of this sector.",""],[1,"148","7","Agricultural Insurance Promotion and Consolidation Policy","There is consensus on the importance of having agricultural insurance at competitive costs and on the need for an important role for the State in promoting and consolidating it.",""],[1,"148","7","Price Insurance and Price-Fixing Strategies","It is possible to generate synergies with different sources of information and with other alternatives for mitigating risk, such as price insurance through price-fixing strategies.",""],[1,"148","7","Multi-Risk Agricultural Insurance Scheme","It is possible to create multi-risk insurance that also improves the sector's commitment, which will make it possible to reduce losses in bad years.",""],[1,"148","8","Aromatic Rice Variety Development Initiative","Finally, the technological aspect linked to the rice sector is connected with the development of grain varieties, mainly in the case of aromatic rice varieties",""],[1,"149","2","Medium- and Short-Grain Variety Development and Market Access Programme","The development of varieties must be accompanied by genetic development, industrial changes to process these types of products, and new markets.",""],[1,"149","3","Commercial Crop Variety Development Research","INIA has an experimental aromatic line, selected together with industry, which achieved very good yield levels, although on a still small scale.",""],[1,"150","3","Organic Meat Development Initiative","In the case of the meat chain, the development of organic meat is highlighted, which constitutes a food niche showing strong growth globally.",""],[1,"150","8","Never Ever 3 Meat Certification","Never Ever 3 certification guarantees that the meat comes from animals that have not received antibiotics, hormones, or proteins of animal origin.",""],[1,"151","2","Industrial Market Development Initiative","First, market development must take place to incentivize industries to produce.",""],[1,"151","4","Non-GMO Soybean Production and Segregation Protocols","The development of non-transgenic (non-GMO) soybean production is viewed as an interesting opportunity, requiring the adaptation of production and segregation protocols to prevent contamination with transgenic soybeans.",""],[1,"152","4","Environmental Differentiation Strategy for Meat Production","The incorporation of information on environmental variables of meat production could constitute an adequate basis for building a differentiation strategy based on environmental quality.",""]],"22":[[1,"115","2","Multisectoral Technological Coordination","Thus, multisectoral technological coordination can be promoted.",""],[1,"115","2","Flexible Smart Irrigation for Renewable Energy Integration","Irrigation systems offer flexibility to the electricity grid, since irrigation can be enabled in real time when there is an energy surplus.",""]],"23":[[1,"127","9","Montevideo Electric Bus Fleet Deployment","The Intendencia de Montevideo has the goal of reaching 100 electric buses or 7% of the fleet by 2019, with an aggressive plan and in agreement with the transport companies.",""]],"24":[[1,"105","5","State Enterprise and Market Regulation Framework","In this transformation, the State, either through its own enterprises or through active regulation and market construction, at the national, regional and global levels, will continue to play a decisive role.",""]],"25":[[1,"152","5","Water Consumption Reduction in Rice Production","It is important to continue reducing water consumption in production.",""],[1,"153","3","Brassica Carinata Biofuel Production Initiative","The option of Brassica carinata, an oilseed specially improved to increase its oil content and unsuitable for human consumption, constitutes an interesting opportunity for winter sowing and another option for continuing to strengthen agricultural rotation.",""],[1,"153","4","Nutrient Circularity Project in Dairy Farms","An example of this is the nutrient circularity project in dairy farms that is being developed within the framework of the Biovalor project.",""],[1,"157","9","Family Farming Promotion and Support Policies","States parties strengthen specific public policies for the promotion and support of family farming and its organizations, based on respect for rural diversity.",""],[1,"171","5","Natural Resource Preservation and Valuation Policy","Preserve and enhance the value of natural resources.",""],[1,"171","5","Sustainable Food Production Development","Generating the conditions for sustainable food production.",""],[1,"171","5","Forest Biomass Value Addition","Generating the conditions for adding value to forest biomass.",""],[1,"171","5","Renewable Energy Utilization","Generating the conditions for the utilization of renewable energies.",""],[1,"171","5","Nature-Based Tourism Promotion","Generating the conditions for nature tourism.",""],[1,"176","10","Integrated Forestry Value-Added Chain Development","A possible example would be to analyse a forestry value-added chain that includes the mechanical treatment of pine for solid wood construction, the chemical treatment of residues to produce long-fibre pulp for paper and cardboard, the generation of bioproducts from the secondary pulping stream as substitutes for petroleum derivatives, and the generation of heat and energy from the process's overall residues.",""]],"26":[[1,"156","5","Incubacoop Cooperative Incubator","In 2016, a cooperative incubator—Incubacoop—began operating to provide technical and financial support for the competitiveness of ventures located in sectors identified as strategic.",""],[1,"156","6","Rural Association Initiatives","Initiatives for rural association",""],[1,"156","11","Cooperative Movement Development and Coordination Space","They have been established as a space for exchange, integration, coordination and development of the cooperative movement rooted in the territory.",""],[1,"160","8","National Productive Transformation and Competitiveness System","The National Productive Transformation and Competitiveness System (Transforma Uruguay) began operating in 2017 with the aim of promoting productive and innovative economic development, with sustainability, social equity, and environmental and territorial balance.",""],[1,"161","2","Transforma Uruguay Multi-Actor Project Facilitation Platform","The way Transforma Uruguay adds value is by substantially enabling or facilitating projects that necessarily involve several institutional actors.",""],[1,"161","3","Cross-Cutting Productive Transformation Projects","A set of cross-cutting projects organized into four areas: internationalization; innovation; capacity development; and the business and investment climate.",""],[1,"161","3","Priority Sector Roadmaps","The vertical dimension through sectoral roadmaps for priority activities, including food, creative industries, forestry and timber, global services and logistics, life sciences, pharmaceuticals and tourism.",""],[1,"161","3","Long-Term Foresight Studies","Foresight studies contribute, through characterization of the dimension or activity concerned in Uruguay, the region and the world, to systematizing the main international trends and constructing relevant long-term scenarios.",""]],"27":[[1,"164","3","Problem-Oriented Scientific and Technological Research Programme","It is necessary that a substantial part of national scientific and technological research focus on solving problems that ultimately generate greater wealth, increase citizens' quality of life, and protect ecosystems.",""],[1,"164","4","Cross-Sectoral Knowledge Generation and Application System","The national scale facilitates a cross-sectoral and multi-stakeholder approach to coordinate policies and agencies, together with the private sector, and thereby design and implement a system for generating and applying knowledge that impacts the country's virtuous transformation.",""],[1,"164","4","Public-Private Development Mission Alliance","Generate a public-private alliance in service of that mission.",""],[1,"165","6","National System of Researchers","The creation of the National System of Researchers (SNI), which, together with other instruments, contributed to promoting scientific research.",""],[1,"173","6","National System of Researchers","National System of Researchers, with the dual objective of identifying and categorizing researchers according to their level of scientific or technological production, and granting them economic incentives that promote professional research activity.",""],[1,"165","6","National Scholarship System","The creation of the National Scholarship System (SNB), which facilitated the training of young researchers.",""],[1,"165","6","Timbó Scientific Bibliography Access Programme","The implementation of the Timbó programme, so that all Uruguayan researchers can access scientific literature.",""],[1,"165","6","Competitive Sectoral Research Funds","The creation of a growing number of competitive sectoral funds.",""],[1,"165","6","Academia–Government Linkage Programmes","The creation of several academia–Government linkage programmes, such as the ANCAP–Udelar days, which were later extended to other public enterprises.",""],[1,"169","3","Expansion of Knowledge Generation Beyond Universities","All actors must accept that part of knowledge generation has to begin taking place in companies and State agencies, as well as in other civil society organizations.",""],[1,"172","3","Scientific Research Professionalization and Training Programme","It is necessary to strengthen the professionalization of scientific research and promote the training of new researchers.",""],[1,"172","3","Competitive Research Project Financing Mechanism","It is necessary to guarantee competitive mechanisms that make it possible to finance research projects.",""],[1,"172","3","Specific Research Equipment Acquisition Support","It is necessary to guarantee competitive mechanisms that make it possible to finance the acquisition of specific equipment.",""],[1,"172","3","Intellectual Property Protection Support Mechanism","It is necessary to guarantee competitive mechanisms that make it possible to finance support for intellectual property protection.",""],[1,"172","3","International Research Cooperation Mechanism","It is necessary to guarantee competitive mechanisms that make it possible to finance international cooperation.",""],[1,"172","3","Non-Academic Researcher Support Instruments","It is a priority to implement instruments so that a significant part of this second objective is carried out by researchers outside the academic sphere.",""],[1,"172","3","Targeted Research Support for Priority Areas and Groups","All instruments, particularly those linked to the training of young researchers, should be accessible to the entire system, while including specific modalities for targeting support.",""],[1,"174","2","Research Incentives Mechanism","Mechanisms shall be implemented to provide incentives that strengthen specific objectives, either permanently or temporarily.",""],[1,"174","2","Non-Academic Researcher Expansion Initiative","And they shall promote growth in the number of researchers and technologists working outside the academic sphere, especially in companies or in the public sector.",""],[1,"174","3","National Scientific Training System","National Scientific Training System for the training of researchers.",""],[1,"174","3","Women’s Scientific Training Incentive","It is also advisable to define specific instruments to encourage the training of women.",""],[1,"174","3","Foreign Youth Training Quota Mechanism","It is also advisable to define specific instruments to encourage the training of women and reserve quotas for foreign young people.",""],[1,"174","3","Overseas Priority-Area Training Programme","Finally, the system should provide instruments to send young people abroad for training in adequately defined priority areas.",""],[1,"174","4","Highly Qualified Diaspora Engagement Plan","Plan for leveraging the highly qualified diaspora.",""],[1,"174","5","Competitive Research Project Funding Funds","Competitive funds for financing fundamental and applied research projects, without prioritized areas.",""],[1,"174","7","Long-Term Priority Research Fund","Fund to finance long-term research in prioritized areas.",""],[1,"175","2","Long-Term Multidisciplinary Financing Mechanism","Maintaining funding for periods of no less than five years, subject to annual evaluation.",""],[1,"175","3","Targeted Research Funding for Weak Scientific Areas","Specific funds to develop research in particularly weak areas, as was done at the time through the creation of PEDECIBA to promote basic sciences.",""],[1,"175","4","Priority Equipment Financing Fund","Equipment financing fund, aimed at the purchase and maintenance of medium- and large-scale equipment in priority areas, seeking its shared use.",""],[1,"175","5","Researcher Exchange and International Cooperation Fund","Fund to promote the exchange of researchers and international cooperation, with different exchange modalities, enabling joint projects that facilitate access to infrastructure unavailable in Uruguay.",""]],"28":[[1,"165","10","Innovation Amendment to Law 19355","Law 19355 of 19 December 2015, amended by Law 19472 of 23 December 2016 to incorporate innovation among its contents.",""],[1,"169","6","Research and Technology Specialization Policy","It is therefore necessary to focus efforts very strongly on those specific areas in which the country may have, or develop, a differentiating characteristic that allows it to successfully insert its products.",""],[1,"171","3","Population-Wide Innovation Capacity Development","Promoting the capacity to innovate throughout the population is therefore not only an unavoidable requirement for inserting the country into the new knowledge society, but also for ensuring that no one is excluded from this development process.",""],[1,"171","8","Society-Wide Innovation Capacity and Entrepreneurship Ecosystem","Promote innovation capacity throughout society and turn Uruguay into a country with a thriving entrepreneurial ecosystem that promotes innovation at both the productive and social levels.",""],[1,"172","4","National Innovation System Formation","Form a national innovation system across all sectors of society, with special emphasis on priority sectors.",""],[1,"175","6","Technology Surveillance and Intellectual Property Protection Office","Independently, the country requires a patent office, or equivalent body, to conduct technological surveillance and foresight, with highly trained technicians in the field.",""],[1,"175","8","Productive Sector Innovation Policy Instruments","Boosting innovation in the productive sector requires defining a set of instruments that take into account the heterogeneity of situations and the different possibilities and interests in innovating.",""],[1,"175","9","Thematic Virtual Research and Innovation Centers","Thematic virtual centers for research, development, innovation and validation of a business model.",""],[1,"175","10","Integration of Virtual Centers into Sectoral Roadmaps","Within the current institutional framework, these virtual centers should be incorporated into the sectoral roadmaps defined and coordinated by the Secretariat for Productive Transformation and Competitiveness.","Secretariat for Productive Transformation and Competitiveness"],[1,"176","2","Knowledge Center Investment and Market Entry Programme","One should invest simultaneously in several of these centers.",""],[1,"176","3","Industrial Extension Center Strengthening Reform","Reformulate and strengthen the Industrial Extension Center to promote business innovation, both in individual firms and through thematic packages.",""],[1,"176","4","Business Digitalization Programme for SMEs","Programme for the digitalization of businesses, particularly SMEs, providing virtual technical assistance and a repository of digital tools.",""],[1,"176","5","Large-Firm Innovation Culture Support Programme","Promoting a culture of innovation in larger companies. These companies would receive support for diagnosing and accompanying the process.",""],[1,"176","6","Technology Park Creation and Investment Incentive Scheme","Creation of technology parks to encourage the establishment of companies with a strong R&D component, particularly in the interior of the country.",""],[1,"176","7","Targeted Investment Promotion and Innovation Subsidy Reform","Review the application of the Investment Promotion Law, seeking greater targeting to favor investments in companies that innovate, eventually granting direct subsidies to ventures undertaking relevant innovations.",""],[1,"176","11","Sectoral Development and Innovation Governance Reform","A different governance is required, with greater state leadership, greater focus on developing new business models and on constructing and testing new development strategies for the sector, more concrete objectives and targets, and naturally, larger budgets.",""],[1,"176","12","Technological Adaptation Plan Development","Recently, it has begun developing a technological adaptation plan.",""],[1,"176","13","SME Digitalization Promotion Programme","A massive programme to boost this digitalisation is needed and is already being launched.",""],[1,"176","15","Commitment-Based Corporate Benefits Mechanism","This type of mechanism already exists, without requiring commitments from the company; current benefits could even be increased, depending on the company's level of commitment.",""],[1,"176","16","Tax Payment Reduction Certificate Scheme","Based on granting certificates that allow reducing payment of taxes (VAT) or BPS.",""],[1,"177","2","Sectoral Transformation Advisory and Support","Bringing them closer to the global state of the art in their sector, advising and supporting the transformations undertaken.",""],[1,"177","3","Foreign Investment Attraction Using Investment Promotion Instruments","Attract foreign direct investment from companies with high innovative standards, using these new instruments of the Investment Promotion Law.",""],[1,"177","4","Innovative Enterprise Public Procurement Incentive Mechanism","Incentives through public procurement to favor national companies that innovate, mainly SMEs and innovative research centers, seeking specific instruments for activities where the impact may be more significant.",""],[1,"177","5","Product Registration and Regulation Capacity Development","Improve product registration and regulation capabilities, following international standards, particularly in life sciences",""],[1,"177","5","Legal and Regulatory Review for Innovation","Review other legal and regulatory instruments to facilitate innovation practice",""],[1,"177","7","Public Research and Innovation Funding Facility","Creation of a specific budget fund intended to finance the R&D&I activities deemed appropriate to undertake",""],[1,"177","8","Stable Public Enterprise Funding for Knowledge Development","Particular impetus to all these activities within the framework of public enterprises, allocating specific and stable budgets for this purpose.",""],[1,"177","10","Researcher Integration into Public Institutions and Enterprises","Incorporation of researchers into public institutions, agencies and enterprises, especially young postdoctoral researchers, particularly in institutions with less innovative momentum.",""],[1,"178","2","Public Policy Innovation Challenges Instrument","Promote instruments of the type of “ANII Challenges” to seek original solutions to identified public policy problems.",""],[1,"178","6","ANII Challenge Instruments","using, for this purpose, instruments such as the “ANII challenges”, among others;",""]],"29":[[1,"168","4","Medium- and Long-Term Science, Technology and Innovation Strategy","The design of an STI Strategy (ECTI) for the medium and long term must be aligned with that of the Development Strategy 2050.",""],[1,"169","5","Results-Oriented Public Policy Development","Advance strongly in results-oriented policies, designed and implemented from knowledge generated and applied to the specific problems they seek to transform.",""],[1,"169","5","Best Available Technology Adoption","Using the best technologies available.",""],[1,"169","5","Public Officials Capacity and Empowerment Programme","With adequately trained, empowered and motivated officials.",""],[1,"169","5","Public Sector Process Reengineering","With a reengineering of processes that makes it possible to reduce inefficiencies and unnecessary costs.",""],[1,"169","5","Policy Monitoring and Evaluation Mechanism","With monitoring and evaluation instruments.",""],[1,"170","3","National Science, Technology and Innovation Planning Framework","This Strategy aims to guide the design of national science, technology and innovation plans to be developed in the coming decades, which should have specific objectives, targets and budgets.",""],[1,"173","3","Permanent Institutionalized Evaluation System","A permanent, institutionalized evaluation system should exist to monitor indicators and issue alerts when an instrument is not meeting its targets.",""],[1,"173","3","Periodic External Audit of Evaluation System","This permanent evaluation, internal to the system, should ultimately be holistically audited periodically by external actors.",""],[1,"176","9","International Expert Leadership Appointment","Possibly hiring a top-level international expert for leadership.",""],[1,"176","14","Technological Surveillance System","implementation of technological surveillance",""],[1,"177","7","Public-Sector Problem Identification Mechanism","Promoting the identification of problems in the public sphere, with the incorporation of an increasing number of bodies",""],[1,"177","7","Public Process Reengineering and Results-Based Management Reform","Particular focus on process reengineering and results-based management",""],[1,"177","13","University-Government Diagnostic Collaboration Mechanism","Following in particular the ANCAP-Udelar or UTE-Udelar model, as well as carrying out external diagnoses for agencies that are not in a position to prepare them internally.",""],[1,"177","14","Ministry and Agency Evaluation and Monitoring Process","The Secretariat for Productive Transformation and Competitiveness has initiated a process of evaluating and monitoring ministries and various agencies.",""],[1,"180","7","Objectives-Based Evaluation System","Instruments of pillar 4 (generate an evaluation system, based on a management-by-objectives model):",""],[1,"180","8","ECTI Implementation Planning Framework","Successive implementation plans for this ECTI must include general and specific objectives, as well as targets with different time horizons.",""],[1,"181","6","ECTI Implementation Planning Framework","The successive plans that implement ECTI shall define the prioritized themes and make them evolve over time.",""],[1,"180","9","Public Policy Instrument Scope and Evaluation Framework","All public policy instruments defined within the framework of the plan must have a predefined scope, indicate the general and specific objectives to which they intend to contribute, and define indicators to evaluate their contribution to the plan's specific target.",""],[1,"180","10","Science, Technology and Innovation Observatory","The system must have an Observatory of Science, Technology and Innovation, including a permanent mechanism for monitoring the various instruments.",""],[1,"180","11","Periodic Second-Level Evaluation and Plan Revision Mechanism","In addition, a second-level evaluation shall be carried out periodically to globally analyze the results of all instruments, compare them with the plan's objectives and targets, and make recommendations for their revision.",""],[1,"180","12","Science, Technology and Innovation Governance Reform","A new Science, Technology and Innovation System requires a structural review of current governance.",""],[1,"181","2","National Science, Technology and Innovation Secretariat Strengthening","the best option would be to strengthen a National Secretariat for Science, Technology and Innovation in the Office of the President, with capacities to design policies and instruments, which would be approved by an Innovation Cabinet chaired by the President of the Republic.",""],[1,"181","3","Multilateral Coordination of Science, Technology and Innovation Policy","The proper implementation of the STI strategy requires greater coordination among all these executors of public funds, so that the set of instruments serves a single national development strategy.",""],[1,"181","4","Renewed and Strengthened Conicyt Advisory Function","The main advisory role will be that of a renewed and strengthened Conicyt, to advise on the design and execution of policies, seeking a virtuous link between the various components of the STI system.",""],[1,"181","4","Independent Conicyt System Audit and Evaluation Mechanism","Conicyt could also fulfill the role of independent auditor of the system, with a small budget to annually hire an external multidisciplinary evaluation team.",""]],"30":[[1,"234","2","Ceibal Plan","The Ceibal Plan has the goal of promoting equity and the democratization of knowledge through narrowing the digital divide",""],[1,"234","2","New Educational Technology Tools","The incorporation of new technological tools for learning",""],[1,"234","4","Student Educational Trajectory Information and Early Warning System","This requires the exchange of information among the institutions through which the student progresses in order to monitor their trajectory and alert them to possible delays and other difficulties.",""],[1,"234","10","National Student Tracking Database (SENDA)","ANEP is developing the National Student Tracking System (SENDA), consisting of a single database containing each student's educational history, the data of the schools in which they were enrolled, their grades, and attendance.","ANEP"],[1,"235","4","Broad Information Technology Literacy Initiative","The requirement to achieve broad literacy in information technologies is also raised.",""]],"31":[[1,"173","2","Permanent Labour Reskilling System","The implementation of a permanent labour reskilling system is required to enable the acquisition of new skills for a constantly evolving production system.",""],[1,"179","5","Future of Work Workforce Reskilling Strategy","Generate a global workforce reskilling strategy for the future of work through the public education system, particularly CETP-UTU, UTEC and Udelar, together with Inefop.",""],[1,"223","4","Lifelong Learning Rights for All Workers","We must imagine a new social contract that guarantees all workers (subordinate, semi-autonomous and independent) the right to lifelong learning.",""],[1,"223","4","Institutional Investment for Future Work Transitions","We must imagine a new social contract that allows increased investment in institutions throughout the transitions entailed by the future of work.",""],[1,"224","4","People-Centered Future of Work Programme","A people-centered programme for the future of work, based on three areas of action.",""],[1,"224","5","Lifelong Learning and Skills Development Policy","The promotion of the right to lifelong learning that enables people to acquire skills, improve them and reskill.",""],[1,"243","2","Labour Productivity and Skills Development Policies","Develop policies aimed at increasing labour productivity, including training and skills development.",""],[1,"243","6","Labor Reskilling and Unemployment Support Systems","Deepen labor reskilling and occupational reconversion systems, articulated with public subsidy systems during episodes of unemployment.",""],[1,"243","7","Labor Reconversion and Reskilling Systems","broad labor reconversion systems must continue to be developed for workers who need to redirect their work activity, both toward new sectors and toward developing new activities in the same sector or company.",""],[1,"243","7","Unemployment and Retraining Subsidy Policies","subsidy policies (for unemployment and retraining) must also be coordinated to enable workers and their families to navigate retraining processes without losing their standard of living.",""],[1,"176","14","PhD-Qualified Personnel Recruitment","For example, hiring personnel with PhDs",""],[1,"176","14","Dual Training Development","development of dual training",""],[1,"174","3","Dual Training Development Mechanism","It is necessary to include specific instruments to promote dual training outside the academic sphere, whether in the public or private sector, including companies and civil society organisations.",""]],"32":[[1,"173","2","Entrepreneurial Ecosystem Promotion Mechanism","It is necessary to promote mechanisms that strengthen the entrepreneurial ecosystem, promoting business incubators, startups and new forms of value generation.",""],[1,"179","7","Entrepreneurial Ecosystem Strengthening Initiative","Strengthen the entrepreneurial ecosystem, complementing ANDE and ANII instruments, seeking to:",""],[1,"179","8","Public and Private Venture Capital Funds","Funds that attract venture capital, both public and private, to enable the scaling of national companies at regional or global level.",""],[1,"179","9","Business Incubators for Startup Creation","Business incubators to promote the creation of startups across a broad spectrum of wealth-generating sectors, linked with universities and the knowledge they develop;",""],[1,"179","10","Frugal Innovation Startup Promotion","Promote the creation of startups focused on frugal innovation, either with a purely commercial objective or to promote social innovation.",""],[1,"179","11","Coworking Spaces and Mini Technology Parks Initiative","promote the creation of coworking spaces and mini technology parks;",""],[1,"179","13","Creativity and Creative Industries Promotion Ecosystem","Generate an ecosystem for promoting creativity and, particularly, creative industries.",""],[1,"180","2","Creative Business Incubators","Creative business incubators.",""],[1,"180","3","Public Creative Laboratories for Experimentation","Public creative laboratories equipped and oriented toward experimentation.",""],[1,"180","4","Product Internationalization Financing Fund","Specific funds to support the internationalization of products, with creative financing mechanisms such as crowdfunding or direct donations from consumers to creative professionals and producers.",""],[1,"180","5","International Promotion of Creative Industries","Promotion of events and spaces to showcase capabilities, services and creative content abroad, bringing them closer to potential demanders, training intermediaries and sales agents for this purpose.",""],[1,"180","6","Innovation Labs and Hackathon Programme","Development of lab or hackathon activities, with a fund for experimentation of winning projects.",""],[1,"179","15","BiliLed Low-Cost Phototherapy Device Development","An example in our country has been the development of BiliLed, a low-cost phototherapy instrument to reduce bilirubin levels in newborn babies.",""]],"33":[[1,"160","6","National Territorial Planning and Sustainable Development Directives","The National Directives for Territorial Planning and Sustainable Development Act proposes defining strategic territorial actions, identifying areas of preferred use, and preparing national programmes that establish coordination and cooperation actions to enable this planning.",""],[1,"196","8","Political Decentralization and Citizen Participation Advancement","El impulso a estos dos aspectos es, entonces, un lineamiento estratégico para seguir avanzando en la superación de las inequidades territoriales.",""],[1,"196","10","Decentralization Bill","The Decentralization Bill currently under discussion in Parliament aims in this direction.",""],[1,"199","4","Territorial Decentralization Based on Complementarity","territorial decentralization based on complementarity",""],[1,"199","4","Integrated Urban Subsystems for Social Services","formation of urban subsystems that integrate social facilities and services",""],[1,"199","5","National Urban Subsystems and Connectivity Corridors","Promote the formation of urban subsystems throughout the country, facilitating the transport of goods and universal access for the population to services and activity areas, while generating corridors and circuits that integrate major social, cultural, recreational and tourism facilities and services at national and international levels.",""],[1,"199","7","Territorial Capacity Optimization and Urban Management","Working within a development framework supported by the national urban system will promote improvements in management toward the construction of sustainable development, seeking to optimize the capacities built in the territory.",""],[1,"199","7","Strategic Planning of New Territorial Facilities","The accurate planning of new facilities.",""],[1,"199","7","Regional Activation of Underused Urban Facilities","At the same time, enhancing those that are underused, thinking in terms of regions rather than cities as a tool to overcome imbalances and bring about the changes promoted by this Strategy.",""],[1,"199","10","National Territorial Planning and Sustainable Development Directives Law","Ley 19525, de Directrices Nacionales de Ordenamiento Territorial y Desarrollo Sostenible.",""],[1,"204","4","Strengthening and Improving Existing Policies","The strategic guidelines prioritize strengthening existing policies and seek to make them even more effective in their reach and impact.",""],[1,"244","6","Infrastructure Investment for Improved Accessibility","Invest in infrastructure to improve accessibility.",""],[1,"244","7","Age-Responsive Urban Infrastructure Adaptation","Adapting urban infrastructure to an older population and people with greater mobility difficulties is another aspect that must be considered in advance.",""],[1,"244","7","Accessible Public and Private Building Design","Buildings specially designed for people with reduced mobility are required in all environments, in both public and private buildings.",""],[1,"244","7","Accessible Urban Transport Systems","Transport systems will also need to be more accessible.",""]],"34":[[1,"237","6","CAIF Early Childhood Care Centres","For early childhood: CAIF centres",""],[1,"237","6","Early Childhood Kindergarten Services","For early childhood: kindergartens",""],[1,"237","6","Socioeducational Inclusion Scholarship Programme","For early childhood: socioeducational inclusion scholarships",""],[1,"237","6","Community Care Homes","For early childhood: community care homes",""],[1,"237","6","Personal Assistant Home Care Service","Regarding people in situations of dependency, the SNIC creates, implements and regulates home care services (Personal Assistants)",""],[1,"237","6","Teleassistance Care Service","Regarding people in situations of dependency, the SNIC creates, implements and regulates care services in the home, Teleassistance",""],[1,"237","6","Day Care Centres for Dependent Persons","Regarding people in situations of dependency, the SNIC creates, implements and regulates care services, day centres",""],[1,"237","6","Long-Term Care Centres for Dependent Persons","Regarding people in situations of dependency, the SNIC creates, implements and regulates care services, long-stay centres",""],[1,"239","2","SNIC Expansion Programme","The second scenario proposes a greater expansion of SNIC, in order to approach universality.",""],[1,"239","2","Personal Assistants Programme Expansion","This scenario is based on expanding the Personal Assistants programme so that it covers 85% of people in a situation of severe dependency.",""],[1,"239","2","Teleassistance Programme Expansion","This scenario is based on expanding the Teleassistance programme to cover 50% of the population with mild or moderate dependency.",""],[1,"241","2","Day Care Centre Service Expansion","new services (day centres) are being created",""],[1,"241","2","Long-Term Care Centre Regulation","other services (long-stay centres) are being regulated",""],[1,"241","2","Health and Care Resource Coordination","it is essential to achieve synergies that allow adequate use of public resources so that health and care policies contribute to the well-being of all people",""],[1,"241","7","Early Childhood SNIC Expansion","Continue expanding SNIC, in its early childhood component in this case.",""]],"35":[[1,"185","2","Societal Capacity Development for Demographic and Technological Change","It is necessary to improve society's capacities to interact with demographic change and increasingly advanced technologies.",""],[1,"242","2","Orderly and Rights-Respecting Immigration Policy","Promote orderly immigration that respects migrants' human rights",""],[1,"242","3","Orderly Immigration and Migrant Integration Policy","It is essential that the social protection system promote orderly immigration and, above all, respect for migrants' human rights, creating the best conditions for their social and labour integration.",""],[1,"244","4","Older Adult-Focused Volunteer Systems","Coordinate broad volunteer systems with a strong focus on older adults",""],[1,"244","5","Retiree Volunteer Engagement Programme","Uruguay's future should not forgo this social energy, full of experience, which, appropriately channelled into volunteer activities adapted to the different profiles and preferences of retired people, can generate social value.",""],[1,"244","8","Health System Adaptation for an Ageing Population","Adaptation of the health system, policies and services to the needs of an increasingly ageing population",""],[1,"245","6","Active Ageing Activity and Participation Policy","Rethink the dividing lines between activity and inactivity in old age",""],[1,"245","7","Social Security Sustainability Review and Reform","It is also necessary, in a complementary manner, to review the sustainability of the social security system.",""],[1,"245","7","Economic Incentives for Older Workers","It is essential to seek mechanisms so that those who reach advanced ages in good health and willing to continue working have economic incentives to do so.",""],[1,"245","7","Flexible Retirement and Part-Time Work Arrangements","It becomes relevant to consider arrangements that allow future older adults greater flexibility to combine the enjoyment of retirement with the possibility of undertaking paid work activities, whether occasional or regular (part-time).",""]],"36":[[1,"214","4","Food Advertising Regulation","The regulation of advertising ... are measures to implement as part of an integrated strategy promoting health.",""],[1,"214","4","Ban on Misleading and Child-Directed Food Advertising","The prohibition of misleading advertising or advertising directed at children ... are measures to implement as part of an integrated strategy promoting health.",""],[1,"214","4","Health Taxes on High-Sodium, High-Fat and High-Sugar Products","The application of taxes to products with high levels of sodium, fats and sugars ... are measures to implement as part of an integrated strategy promoting health.",""],[1,"214","5","Inclusive Public Spaces and Physical Activity Equipment Expansion","This also requires continuing to increase the availability of inclusive public spaces and equipment that facilitate accessibility for the entire population, in all neighborhoods and localities.",""],[1,"214","5","Bicycle Transport Promotion and Private Car Disincentives","Promoting the use of bicycles as a means of transport and discouraging individual car use are part of this strategy.",""],[1,"214","5","Physical Activity Promotion Regulations","The implementation of regulations that promote physical activity in the most diverse settings or institutions has already made progress in educational centers, but must be generalized in that sphere and extended to other spaces, such as workplaces.",""],[1,"214","6","Women-Focused Tobacco Control Campaigns","The continuity of public policies against smoking will require consideration of the high prevalence of consumption among women, with campaigns specifically directed at them.",""],[1,"214","8","Healthy Environment Policy Strengthening","Regarding the interaction between health and the environment, public policies for creating and protecting healthy environments need to be strengthened through promotion, prevention and mitigation measures.",""],[1,"245","2","Sociocultural Health Determinants Policy Approach","Development of an approach to the sociocultural determinants of health through the strengthening of public policies",""],[1,"245","3","Healthy Food Regulation Programme","The policy options include promoting healthy eating by regulating high levels of sodium, fats and sugars.",""],[1,"245","3","Tobacco Control Strategy Continuity","The policy options include ensuring the continuity of the strategy related to tobacco use.",""],[1,"245","3","Alcohol Harm and Dependency Policy","The policy options include regulating supply and developing a comprehensive policy for problematic alcohol use and dependency.",""],[1,"245","3","Physical Activity and Inclusive Public Spaces Programme","The policy options include reducing sedentary behaviour by promoting healthy physical activity through inclusive public spaces and equipment that facilitates accessibility for the entire population.",""],[1,"245","3","Environmental Care Promotion Initiative","The policy options include promoting environmental care.",""],[1,"245","5","Health Prevention and Promotion Programmes","This model emphasizes prevention and promotion, and action on the determinants of disease and also of health.",""]],"37":[[1,"213","9","Health Service and Workforce Transformation Reform","Thus, the health system must anticipate these trends and transform its service offer and human resources to provide an adequate response.",""],[1,"215","7","Health Care Model Transformation Continuation","Finally, a third factor will determine the future outcome of the health system and the population's health status: continuity in the process of transforming the care model.",""],[1,"216","3","Territorial Decentralization of Primary Health Care","Territorial decentralization must continue to be promoted through a Primary Health Care strategy that ensures population assignment to health teams with a family and community focus.",""],[1,"216","3","Integration of High-Complexity Hospitals into Primary Care","High-complexity sanatoriums and hospitals are integrated into the Primary Health Care strategy as referral centers for resolving complex pathologies and hosting diagnostic and treatment services.",""],[1,"216","3","National Integrated Emergency System","Particular attention is warranted for rationalizing emergency, urgent-care, and transfer systems toward their articulation in a National Integrated Emergency System.",""],[1,"216","4","Primary Health Care Capacity Development Programme","Work to achieve greater resolution capacity among basic health teams, with adequate continuous training and efficient interaction with other levels.",""],[1,"216","4","High-Complexity Health Resource Complementation","Greater complementation of high-complexity diagnostic and therapeutic resources should be promoted.",""],[1,"217","4","PIAS Oral and Mental Health Benefits Expansion","Progress shall be made towards 2050 in comprehensiveness by expanding the set of PIAS benefits in oral health and mental health.",""],[1,"217","4","National Mental Health Plan Guidance","The National Mental Health Plan, within the framework of Law 19,529, will offer clear guidance in that direction.",""],[1,"217","5","Participatory Health Planning Mechanism","Participatory planning on prioritized problems in territorial and institutional settings",""],[1,"217","5","Social Accountability Mechanism Strengthening","Strengthening social accountability mechanisms",""],[1,"217","5","Patient Rights and Shared Decision-Making in Care","Humanization of treatment, respect for users' rights and their decision-making capacity regarding the care they receive",""],[1,"217","5","Health Team and Community Care Linkage Strengthening","Strengthening the link between the health team and patients, families and communities, on the basis of adequate care times and continuity of care",""],[1,"217","6","Health Workforce Curriculum Adaptation","Health personnel training must adapt to these changes, adjusting undergraduate and postgraduate curricula within the framework of a National Health Human Resources Plan.",""],[1,"217","6","Continuous Health Workforce Training Programme","Continuous training should be prioritized.",""],[1,"217","6","Geographic Redistribution of Health Personnel","The geographical distribution of personnel should also be adjusted, as a condition for equitable access to care.",""],[1,"217","6","Collaborative Health Research Agenda","The development of a health research agenda is also considered relevant, linking academia with the health system and communities.",""],[1,"217","7","Health System Stewardship and Consolidation Reform","Finally, the stewardship of the Ministry of Public Health and the consolidation of the National Integrated Health System are essential to advance the points mentioned above.","Ministry of Public Health (MSP)"],[1,"218","3","Health System Redesign","redesign health systems",""],[1,"218","3","Intersectoral Health Determinants Policies","promote active intersectoral policies on the social, environmental and economic determinants of health",""],[1,"245","4","Primary Health Care Model Transformation","Continue transforming the health care model, progressively prioritizing primary health care.",""],[1,"245","5","Integrated Primary Health Care Services Model","Public health policies must prioritize the construction of an integrated model that responds to a primary health care strategy based on integrated health service networks.",""],[1,"245","5","Health Programmes and Plans Development","It goes beyond merely responding to demand, and develops health programmes and plans.",""],[1,"245","5","Rational Technology and Medicines Use Regulation","It regulates and promotes the rational use of technology and medicines.",""]],"38":[[1,"216","4","Health Technology Assessment and Incorporation Mechanism","Ensure continuity between health technology assessment mechanisms and decision-making for its incorporation into the Comprehensive Health Care Plan (PIAS), as well as monitoring of implementation.",""],[1,"216","4","National Health Technology Policy and Regulatory Framework","It is therefore essential to continue advancing towards a national policy for the incorporation, creation and review of technology, with robust regulatory support.",""],[1,"216","5","Telemedicine Regulatory Framework","The creation of a regulatory framework for the development of telemedicine that protects physicians in the practice of this activity.",""],[1,"216","5","Digital Self-Monitoring Access Policy","The development of public policies that facilitate access to continuous self-monitoring devices for people with lower incomes.",""],[1,"216","5","Digital Skills Training for Non-Native Users","The development of public policies that train non-natives in information and communication technologies, democratizing the benefits of new technologies.",""],[1,"216","6","Health Record Data Availability Initiative","Promote the free availability of HCEN data, with due protection of sensitive personal data, to users, providers and",""],[1,"217","2","Information Repository for Evidence-Based Decision-Making","Developing an information repository with fundamental data for decision-making.",""],[1,"217","2","ICT and Health Curriculum Reform for Medical Training","Curricula for future doctors should be reviewed to provide a greater range of subjects related to ICT and health.",""],[1,"217","2","ICT Training Programme for Administrative Staff","Programmes to train administrative staff in ICT, so that labour reconversion occurs without loss of jobs.",""],[1,"217","3","Medical Technology Development Programme","It will be important for the future of the ICT and health ecosystem to stimulate the development of medical technology in the country.",""],[1,"217","3","Health Technology Data Governance Framework","For this purpose, appropriate regulatory frameworks must be established, in order to limit data leakage abroad in the event of Big Tech entering the sector.",""],[1,"217","3","Technology-Intensive Public Health Infrastructure Investment","Accompanying these actions, public investment in health should be directed toward more technology-intensive infrastructure.",""],[1,"217","7","Epidemiological Information and Surveillance Strengthening","Information and epidemiological surveillance systems may be strengthened through the use of the National Electronic Health Record to strengthen decision-making in the design and monitoring of policies and plans.",""],[1,"218","2","Rapid Response to Emerging and Communicable Diseases","health, including rapid responses to emerging pathologies or communicable diseases and vectors.",""]],"39":[[1,"230","4","Cultural Rights Policies for Vulnerable Groups","the formulation and implementation of policies aimed at the most vulnerable people and groups who may see their capacities to exercise these rights reduced",""],[1,"168","2","Private Financing Mobilization Process","It is imperative to initiate a process that allows significantly increasing financing of private origin.",""],[1,"171","9","Cross-Cutting Systemic Integration of Four Guidelines","These four guidelines must be interrelated transversally through a systemic approach in order to achieve their maximum enhancement, particularly the first two with each other and the last with the other three.",""],[1,"177","9","Social Policy Innovation Initiative","Particular impetus to innovation in social policies, seeking a problem-focused approach through a multidisciplinary and transdisciplinary approach involving academics, public and private actors, and civil society.",""],[1,"178","3","Private-Sector Participation in Public Policy Innovation","Involve private actors associated with specific public policies in innovation processes.",""],[1,"178","4","Permanent Academic Advisory Forum for Policy Design","Generate a permanent forum for advice from the academic community, particularly through the National Academy of Sciences, to promote understanding of major technological, environmental, social and cultural megatrends, among others, and enable this knowledge to be incorporated into public policy design.",""],[1,"178","5","Civil Society Innovation Mobilization Initiative","Promoting innovation activity with civil society and its organizations, seeking in particular to mobilize scientific and technological capabilities to address social, environmental, cultural, territorial, and coexistence challenges.",""],[1,"178","7","Co-Creation and Co-Design Participation Mechanism","Generating new modalities of participation through co-creation and co-design instances of solutions.",""]],"40":[[1,"246","7","Enhanced Direct Income Transfer and Family Benefits System","It is necessary to strengthen direct income transfers to the poorest, to guarantee minimum incomes for those living in poverty and stop the decline in the incomes and consumption capacity of those in vulnerable situations.",""],[1,"246","8","Public Social Services Expansion","Expand the supply and coverage of public social services",""],[1,"247","5","Basic Public Services Benefits Package and Quality Equalization","A key component of this definition is linked to what the basic package of services and benefits provided in each service is and to reducing territorial and subsystem stratification, with differences in quality that especially harm lower-income groups.",""],[1,"247","7","Universal Social Protection Service Quality Assurance Framework","Finally, a fundamental element of the commitment to a universal social protection system is the definition of standards for quality assurance of educational, health and care services, and the development of a roadmap to advance in that direction.",""],[1,"248","2","Structural Inequality-Sensitive System Design and Targeted Policies","Recognize structural inequalities and consider them in the design of the system, while maintaining, as a complement, targeted policies.",""],[1,"248","3","Non-Contributory Social Protection Floor","The non-contributory pillar of social protection should be the minimum floor",""],[1,"248","3","Contributory Social Protection Complement","The contributory pillar should complement this base",""],[1,"248","3","Targeted Social Protection Programmes for Vulnerable Sectors","Targeted action remains—and must remain—a core part of the policy framework for vulnerable sectors",""],[1,"248","3","Sectoral Policy and Targeted Programme Coordination Mechanism","Combating some entrenched pockets of poverty and inequality requires a fluid link between sectoral policy and targeted programmes",""],[1,"249","5","Early Childhood Investment within Universal Social Protection System","Achieve a social protection system that accompanies people's life cycle, prioritizing investment in early childhood.",""]],"41":[[1,"246","9","Basic Health and Education Service Expansion","expand the basic provision",""],[1,"247","2","Expanded Health Service Supply","In the case of health services, expanding provision should be associated with extending service hours",""],[1,"247","2","Extended Health Service Hours","extending service hours—compatible with paid and unpaid work",""],[1,"247","2","Expanded Health Benefits for Specific Groups","expanding benefits for specific groups",""],[1,"247","2","Integrated Health Care Service Expansion","expanding integrated services under the Comprehensive Health Care Plan",""],[1,"247","2","Reduction of Economic Barriers to Health Care","reducing economic barriers to access (fees and tickets)",""]],"42":[[1,"247","6","Public Transport Access Policy","Policies that facilitate people’s access to services—such as public transport—are central to guaranteeing similar access conditions for all citizens.",""]],"43":[[1,"248","5","Universal Ethnic-Racial Equality Policies","Develop universal policies sensitive to ethnic-racial differences and inequalities.",""],[1,"248","6","Afro-Descendant Inclusion in Policy Targeting","It is necessary to make Afro-descendant people visible among the target population of each policy.",""],[1,"248","6","Multiethnic Representation in State Institutions","The visibility of the Afro-descendant population also requires that the image the State projects of itself and of society reflect the multiethnic character of the Uruguayan population.",""],[1,"248","8","Mainstreaming Racial Equity Across Public Policies","It is essential to integrate mainstreaming, comprehensive, prospective planning, territorial and intersectional approaches into public policies aimed at promoting racial equity.",""],[1,"249","2","Affirmative Action Measures","Deepen the implementation of affirmative action measures",""],[1,"249","3","Affirmative Action in Education and Employment","Deepening affirmative action in the educational and labor areas, as established in Law 19122.",""],[1,"249","3","Anti-Racism Education Policy Formulation","The racial gaps identified in the education system require the formulation of public policies that counteract both the negative impacts of structural racism and the dynamics of institutional racism that expel Afro-descendant people from the system.",""],[1,"249","4","Afro-Descendant Professional Training and Labour Reskilling Measures","Measures should be considered to include professional training and labour reskilling processes that enable the diversification of Afro-descendant people's integration into the labour market.",""]],"44":[[1,"248","7","Housing Programme Access Guidance","providing guidance and advice on access to housing programmes",""],[1,"248","7","Afro-Descendant Priority in Housing Selection","giving weight to Afro-descendant ancestry in the selection of households benefiting from such programmes",""],[1,"248","7","Rental Guarantee Access Support","facilitating access to rental guarantees",""],[1,"248","7","Housing Renovation and Construction Assistance","facilitating access to credit or materials for renovation and construction",""],[1,"248","7","Afro-Descendant Cooperative Housing Support","supporting cooperative housing processes in Afro-descendant communities",""]],"45":[[1,"256","2","Multi-Stakeholder Agreement and Shared Agenda Mechanism","It seems essential to bring together visions and proposals from different social and political actors so that aspirations can crystallize into effective public policies.",""],[1,"279","5","Gender Equality State Policy","Assume the gender equality agenda as a state policy.",""],[1,"279","5","Integrated Gender Equality Regulatory Framework","Generate a comprehensive and coordinated regulatory framework for gender equality.",""],[1,"279","5","Gender Equality Mainstreaming Across Government and Territories","Advance the mainstreaming of the gender equality agenda in the State and in the territories, with a focus on the interior of the country.",""],[1,"279","5","Gender Equality Training for Public Officials","Strengthen the capacities of public officials through gender equality courses integrated into ongoing training and human resources management throughout its entire cycle.",""],[1,"279","5","Gender Capacity Integration in Public Policy-Making","Incorporate these capacities into public policy-making processes, and not only into the internal processes of public bodies.",""],[1,"279","7","Gender Institutional Mainstreaming Reform","Consolidate gender institutionalization in the State to guarantee mainstreaming in other institutions and in the policies and programmes they develop.",""],[1,"279","7","Institutional Gender Action Protocols","Specific action protocols should also be established in the short term for each institution.",""],[1,"279","7","Civil Society and Academic Participation in Gender Governance","The active and systematic participation of civil society organizations and academia in the National Gender Council should also be guaranteed.",""],[1,"283","5","Gender Equality Legal and Institutional Frameworks","the legal and institutional frameworks that are established",""],[1,"283","5","Cross-Sectoral Alliances for Gender Equality","the possible alliances among key actors from the State, civil society and academia, the private sector, the media and citizens as a whole",""]],"46":[[1,"260","3","Institutional Strengthening for Women's Employment Access","Institutions that enable women's access to employment must be strengthened.",""],[1,"260","3","Measures to Combat Occupational Gender Segregation","Combating vertical and horizontal segregation.",""],[1,"260","3","Equal Labour Income Policy","Pursuing equality of labour income.",""],[1,"278","4","Women’s Personal and Employment Development Strategy","strategies to provide these women with opportunities for personal and employment development",""],[1,"280","17","Integrated Women's Economic Empowerment Policy Framework","An integrated policy framework should be developed to advance women's economic empowerment.",""],[1,"280","18","Economic Resource Equality Regulatory Reform","Adapt norms and regulations to promote equality in access to and control of economic resources.",""],[1,"281","2","Corporate Equality Behaviour Promotion Policy","Promote behaviours that support equality in companies.",""],[1,"281","3","Women Entrepreneurs’ Access Facilitation Initiative","Facilitate women's access to infrastructure, technology, credit and marketing.",""],[1,"281","7","Regulatory Reform for Formalizing Women-Led Small Businesses","Review regulations for the formalization of small businesses led by women, with the purpose of overcoming perverse incentives to remain in small-scale ventures because expansion requires paying more taxes and losing social benefits.",""],[1,"281","13","Equal Access to Asset Ownership and Development Opportunities","It is proposed to incentivize equal access to ownership of assets and development opportunities.",""],[1,"281","13","Differentiated Credit and Technical Assistance Measures for Women","Design differentiated measures for women's access to credit and technical assistance.",""],[1,"281","13","Women’s Training and Labor Initiative Development","Strengthen women's training and labor or productive initiatives.",""],[1,"281","13","Female Business Leadership Development","Strengthen female business leadership.",""],[1,"281","14","Gender-Equal Decent Employment Policy","Ensure that women of all ethnic-racial backgrounds and different ages have access to decent employment on equal terms and without any discrimination. This includes equal pay and reducing occupational segregation.",""],[1,"282","2","Women's Formal Employment Integration Policy","the integration of women into the formal sector of the economy",""],[1,"282","2","Workplace Harassment Prevention and Response Measures","prevent and address situations of harassment",""],[1,"282","4","Rural Women's Agricultural Inclusion and Productive Integration","Promote the inclusion of women in all agricultural productive and labour spheres, which entails addressing the demands of rural women, such as recognizing their social security rights and promoting their productive integration, among others.",""]],"47":[[1,"265","7","Women, Science and Technology Strategy","In December 2016, the Government launched the interinstitutional and intersectoral Women, Science and Technology strategy, which seeks precisely to influence the determinants of educational trajectories in order to reverse gender inequalities in the fields of science, technology, engineering and mathematics, and their resulting impact on the country's development.",""],[1,"280","3","Workforce Qualification Enhancement Programme","it is necessary to increase the qualification level of workers",""],[1,"280","3","Scientific and Technological Skills Training","greater training is necessary in different scientific and technological areas",""]],"48":[[1,"280","5","Human Rights and Non-Discrimination Education Programme","Universalize education in human rights, gender equality and non-discrimination in the formal education system.",""],[1,"280","6","Gender Equality and Human Rights Training Programme","Train public officials, teachers, and others in gender equality and human rights",""],[1,"280","8","Educational Relationship Promotion Strategies","Implement strategies in the educational sphere to promote relationships free of",""],[1,"280","12","Gender Equality and Rights in Educational Curricula","Prioritize, in educational curricula, the theme of gender equality and rights.",""]],"49":[[1,"281","5","Gender Stereotype Elimination Policy","Dismantle gender stereotypes.",""],[1,"281","6","Women's Organization and Voice Initiative","Guarantee organization and voice for women.",""],[1,"282","6","Gender Stereotype Elimination Strategies","The development of clear and decisive strategies to achieve the cultural change involved in eliminating gender stereotypes.",""],[1,"282","7","Cultural Transformation for Gender Equality","Promote cultural transformation toward gender equality in households and society, involving women and men in their broadest diversity.",""],[1,"282","8","Institutional Engagement to Challenge Patriarchal Norms","Involve the various institutional socializing agents in questioning and denaturalizing the patriarchal system, particularly its classist, adult-centered, heteronormative, and racist components.",""],[1,"282","9","Gender Stereotype Deconstruction and Diversity Promotion","Promote the deconstruction of traditional gender stereotypes, recognizing diverse models of being a woman and being a man.",""],[1,"282","10","Cultural Rights and Diversity Promotion Actions","promote actions for the exercise of cultural rights and respect for cultural diversity",""],[1,"282","10","Gender Equality Cultural Change Initiative","the institutional communication channels, as well as the different media, have an active commitment to cultural change towards gender equality",""]],"50":[[1,"282","11","Universal Sexual and Reproductive Health Access","ensure universal access to comprehensive and respectful sexual and reproductive health care for women and men, with or without disabilities",""],[1,"283","2","Informed Reproductive Decision-Making Promotion","Promote informed reproductive decisions for the development of free and responsible motherhood and fatherhood, seeking to prevent unintended adolescent pregnancy.",""],[1,"283","2","Nationwide Access to Voluntary Pregnancy Termination","Guarantee effective access to voluntary termination of pregnancy throughout the national territory, with quality services.",""]],"51":[[1,"283","3","Legal and Legislative Framework Update","the updating of regulatory and legislative frameworks",""],[1,"283","3","Protection and Justice Access Initiative","guaranteeing access to protection and justice for women, girls, boys and adolescents",""],[1,"283","3","Gender-Based Violence Prevention and Reparations Programme","prevention, care, protection and reparation by the State, civil society organizations and the community",""],[1,"283","3","Rights Exercise and Autonomy Support","restoring opportunities for the effective exercise of their rights in achieving their autonomy",""],[1,"291","5","First National Prevalence Survey on Gender-Based Violence","First National Prevalence Survey on Gender-Based Violence","MIDES"]],"52":[[1,"283","4","Vulnerable Women Housing Solutions Programme","Guarantee housing solutions for women in the most vulnerable sectors.",""],[1,"283","4","Inclusive and Sustainable Public Spaces Initiative","Promote inclusive, accessible and sustainable public spaces.",""],[1,"283","4","Gender-Responsive Sustainable Development Actions","Generate actions toward sustainable development from an economic, social, environmental and gender perspective.",""]],"53":[[1,"258","8","Productive Matrix Transformation and Productivity Policy","The transformation of the productive matrix proposed in this 2050 Development Strategy seeks to increase overall productivity levels of the economy and, in particular, reduce the enormous productivity differences between sectors and activities.",""],[1,"291","8","Entrepreneurial Venture Identification and Promotion Project","Project for the identification and promotion of entrepreneurial ventures","MIEM"],[1,"294","20","Uruguay Transforms: Food Sector Science, Technology and Innovation Roadmap","Uruguay Transforms. Roadmap in science, technology and innovation for the food sector.",""]]}});